{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017UnikfRZFGuoPHSRajX4j4","type":"tool_result","content":"2016 PLAN.md\n1:# MASH TV\n26:## 0. Quick facts\n40:## 1. Ground rules for the builder\n68:## 2. What makes Smash TV distinctive, and how MASH TV makes it play\n88:## 3. The game at a glance\n109:## 4. Controls and input\n111:### 4.1 Bindings\n129:### 4.2 Engine input presets\n159:### 4.3 How a contestant reads its intent each step\n179:### 4.4 Prompts and glyphs\n200:## 5. Systems and mechanics\n205:### 5.1 Contestants (the players)\n250:### 5.2 Weapons and power-ups\n276:### 5.3 Pickups and economy\n306:### 5.4 Ratings (the show's heartbeat)\n332:### 5.5 Arena, doors and hazards\n379:### 5.6 Room flow (phases)\n403:### 5.7 Waves: the room script data format\n431:### 5.8 Enemies\n470:### 5.9 Bosses\n566:### 5.10 Scoring, lives, continue, high scores\n583:### 5.11 Difficulty and player scaling\n589:### 5.12 The broadcast layer (how the show talks)\n606:## 6. Content overview\n621:### 6.1 Every episode uses the same map shape\n650:## 7. Episode and room content\n652:### 7.1 EPISODE 1: THE PILOT (Studio 9, set `studio`)\n722:### 7.2 EPISODE 2: SWEEPS WEEK (the MegaMart Prize Warehouse, set `warehouse`)\n782:### 7.3 EPISODE 3: THE SEASON FINALE (the Rooftop Gala, set `rooftop`, at night)\n845:### 7.4 THE GREEN ROOM (bonus, set `greenroom`)\n857:### 7.5 THE LIGHTNING ROUND (AI Hub sessions only)\n866:### 7.6 Prizes (§5.3) and Penny's joke for each\n900:## 8. Story beats and script\n912:### 8.1 Cold Open (after the lobby)\n929:### 8.2 Episode beats\n957:### 8.3 Enemy introductions (the first appearance in a run doubles as the tutorial)\n971:### 8.4 Line pools (random without repeats; rate-limited by §5.12)\n1014:## 9. Presentation: art direction, assets, animation, effects\n1016:### 9.1 Art direction\n1039:### 9.2 Sets (one per episode, plus the Green Room)\n1055:### 9.3 Characters\n1079:### 9.4 New art assets to author (list them in `src/06-