{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013FTyUAsoncSkwaKFhDMoR5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# MASH TV\n2\t\n3\t*A playful riff on Smash TV. I brainstormed fifty riffs on the source's name and numbered them, then drew one with Python's\n4\t`secrets.randbelow(50) + 1`. It came up 9: **MASH TV**. Don't re-pick the title.*\n5\t\n6\t**Pitch.** MASH TV is a 1–4 player twin-stick arena shooter set inside the deadliest game show on television. Contestants\n7\tfight through single-screen studio rooms while goons, robots and worse pour in through four doors. They grab cash and\n8\tridiculous prizes, play to the cameras to keep the **ratings** up, and pick a route through the studio map. The goal is to\n9\tsurvive three episodes, each capped by a giant boss, and reach the Season Finale. Collect enough Golden Keys and the\n10\tsecret **Green Room** opens at the end. Your host is the immortal, oily, sequinned **Lance Lustre**: *\"KA-CHING! KA-BOOM!\"*\n11\t\n12\t**Names and files** (use the model id and timestamp from *your* TASK.md):\n13\t\n14\t| What | Value |\n15\t|---|---|\n16\t| Title on screen | `MASH TV` (sub-line: `LIVE FROM STUDIO 9`) |\n17\t| GameTitle in file names | `MashTV` |\n18\t| SOURCE in file names | `SmashTV` |\n19\t| Dev folder (all dev files) | `MashTV-SmashTV-<model>-<timestamp>/` |\n20\t| Deliverable (root, beside TASK.md) | `MashTV-SmashTV-<model>-<timestamp>.html` |\n21\t| Exit interview (root, beside the HTML) | `exit-interview.json` |\n22\t| \"Plan\" field in Source Information | `PLAN.md` |\n23\t\n24\t---\n25\t\n26\t## 0. Quick facts\n27\t\n28\t| | |\n29\t|---|---|\n30\t| Genre | Twin-stick arena shooter (arcade). Co-op for 1–4 players, with a route choice between rooms. |\n31\t| Perspective | One fixed single-screen arena per room, seen from a high three-quarter \"studio camera\": the engine view `threequarter` (pitch 55). `topdown` (pitch 80) is a Settings option. |\n32\t| Engine | my-3D2dge handoff package **v0.85.2** (`github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge`, `dist/handoff/`; commit `4390a98` when planned). Use the full edition, `my-3d2dge.js`, which includes every module (we use `arcade`). |\n33\t| Online | AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client `aihub-session 1.4.0`, **mode `shared-world`**, 1–4 players. |\n34\t| Local multiplayer | 1–4 players on one screen: P1 on keyboard+mouse or a pad, P2–P4 on pads (drop-in with Options/Start). |\n35\t| Length | A full run takes about 20–25 minutes: three episodes of 2–4 rooms plus a boss, then the bonus Green Room. A hub session round takes about 5–6 minutes. |\n36\t| Output | One self-contained HTML file with the engine, the hub client and the game inlined. No image or audio files; everything is drawn and synthesized in code. |\n37\t\n38\t---\n39\t\n40\t## 1. Ground rules for the builder\n41\t\n42\t1. **TASK.md is the contract; this plan is how to meet it.** Where they disagree, TASK.md wins.\n43\t2. **Work only inside your dev folder.** Other agents share the parent directories, ports and processes. Read nothing\n44\t   outside your folder except what you fetch:\n45\t   - Engine: shallow-clone it **inside your dev folder** (e.g. `.cache/my-3d2dge`; when this plan was written, `/tmp` on this\n46\t     machine was a full tmpfs) with `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge .cache/my-3d2dge`.\n47\t     Copy `dist/handoff/*` into the dev folder: the engine, the docs, the tools, the kits and `src/assets`.\n48\t   - Hub: **don't clone ai-hub** (it's over 1 GB). Fetch the four files you need:\n49\t     `curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/{session.js,harness.html,bridge.js,round.js}`\n50\t     into `vendor/hub/`. `lib/hub/README.md` is the protocol; read it once, whole.\n51\t3. **Servers and processes.** Prefer `file://` and headless Node. The hub harness needs a server: bind `127.0.0.1` on port 0\n52\t   (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints the port, or a Node `http` server on port 0). Before trusting a\n53\t   result, check that the page is your game (`window.MT` exists and the title is `MASH TV`). Stop only processes you\n54\t   started, by PID. Never use `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\n55\t4. **Read the engine docs before writing code.** Read `API.md` whole. Read `docs/ASSETS.md` whole before drawing props.\n56\t   Grep `API-INDEX.md` for names; read the `AI_GUIDE.md` sections on Standard features, Frame order, Players, Testing\n57\t   and the Twin-stick recipe. Every API name in this plan was checked against v0.85.2. If your copy is newer, grep the index.\n58\t5. **Engine patches are allowed but kept small**, each listed with its reason in `engine/PATCHES.md`. That list feeds the\n59\t   Engine Feedback. The patches this plan needs are in §15.5.\n60\t6. **No TODOs, placeholders, stubs or \"coming soon\" anywhere.** Every menu item works; every feature in this plan ships.\n61\t7. **One test command** (`npm test` → `node tools/test.mjs`) prints only failures and a one-line count. Rerun only the\n62\t   suites whose code you changed (`--only <suite>`), and run everything before you hand off. Use screenshots only for\n63\t   what a script can't check (§17.3). As TASK.md says, don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or\n64\t   audit.\n65\t\n66\t---\n67\t\n68\t## 2. What makes Smash TV distinctive, and how MASH TV makes it play\n69\t\n70\t| Source trait | MASH TV mechanic or feature |\n71\t|---|---|\n72\t| A lethal TV game show played as entertainment, with a smarmy host | **Lance Lustre** reacts to everything on a **jumbotron** above the arena, with a lower-third subtitle and gibberish voice. The **Ratings** system turns \"be entertaining\" into a mechanic: it drives a cash multiplier, Prime Time, and producer \"stunts\" when you dawdle. |\n73\t| Hordes flooding in through four doors | Door-spawn wave director: each door opens, enemies pour through and the door slams shut. Up to ~60 enemies on screen. |\n74\t| Two-stick 8-way shooting while moving | Analog twin-stick (pad), mouse aim (PC), and 8-way arrow-key fire (keyboard only). |\n75\t| Power-ups, cash and absurd consumer prizes | Timed weapons, cash × the ratings multiplier, and named joke prizes (\"A SELF-AWARE TOASTER\"). Co-host **Penny Prize** tallies them in a Prize Recap after each episode. |\n76\t| A room-to-room map with path choice | Episode maps (3×3 grid). After a clear, the exits light up with the destination's name; walk through one to choose. Longer paths hold keys and cash; shorter paths carry less risk. |\n77\t| Giant, multi-part bosses | **Mashy** the mascot (shoot off its parts), the **Wheel of Misfortune** (each spin picks the attack), **Lance in the Starmaker 9000**, then **The Network** itself. |\n78\t| A secret bonus for collectors | **Golden Keys** (9 in the game). With 5 or more after the finale, you reach the **Green Room** and the true ending. |\n79\t| Simultaneous co-op | 1–4 players in one arena, locally or online (AI Hub shared world). Ratings and keys are shared; cash is individual. |\n80\t\n81\t**Tone:** loud, garish and cartoon-violent. Enemies burst into **confetti, sparks and smoke** (no blood: \"BY ORDER OF THE\n82\tFCC, ALL GORE HAS BEEN REPLACED WITH CONFETTI!\"). It's consumerist satire with a retro-future TV aesthetic: neon, chrome,\n83\tmarquee bulbs, sponsor logos. **Writing style:** short, shouted, ALL-CAPS announcer lines with punchlines and fake sponsor\n84\tplugs, like the source's barker energy. Every line is original (§8).\n85\t\n86\t---\n87\t\n88\t## 3. The game at a glance\n89\t\n90\t**Core loop (one sentence):** enter a sealed studio room, survive the waves pouring from its doors while grabbing cash,\n91\tprizes and power-ups, then pick the next door on the studio map, until you reach and beat the episode's boss.\n92\t\n93\t**Flow:**\n94\t\n95\t```\n96\tBoot ─► Title ─(10 s idle)─► Attract demo ─(any input)─► Title\n97\tTitle menu: START THE SHOW · EPISODES · HOW TO PLAY · TOP EARNERS · OPTIONS · ABOUT & CREDITS\n98\tSTART THE SHOW ─► Difficulty ─► Contestant Lobby (join 1–4) ─► Cold Open ─► Episode 1 card\n99\t  ─► Room ─► (clear) ─► choose exit ─► \"NEXT ON MASH TV\" map card ─► Room … ─► Boss ─► Prize Recap\n100\t  ─► Episode 2 card … Boss ─► Prize Recap ─► Episode 3 card … Finale (Lance ─► The Network) ─► Prize Recap\n101\t  ─► keys ≥ 5 ? Green Room ─► Ending B (true ending) : Ending A\n102\t  ─► Initials (each qualifying player) ─► Top Earners ─► Title\n103\tAll lives lost (every player out) ─► CONTINUE? 10…0 (✕/Enter: continue, −50 % winnings) ─► else Game Over ─► Initials ─► Top Earners ─► Title\n104\tAI Hub session: Our own card (contestant line-up) ─► 3-2-1 ─► Lightning Round (3 rooms + Mashy) ─► finish ─► end card\n105\t```\n106\t\n107\t---\n108\t\n109\t## 4. Controls and input\n110\t\n111\t### 4.1 Bindings\n112\t\n113\t| Action | DualSense (default glyphs) | Xbox glyphs (Settings) | Keyboard + mouse |\n114\t|---|---|---|---|\n115\t| Move | L-stick, D-pad | L-stick, D-pad | W A S D |\n116\t| Aim + fire | R-stick (fires while pushed past 0.35) | R-stick | Mouse aims (reticle); **hold Left click** fires |\n117\t| Fire (in the last aim direction) | R2 (hold) | RT | — |\n118\t| 8-way fire (keyboard only) | — | — | Arrow keys (hold; two arrows = diagonal) |\n119\t| Slide (dodge with i-frames) | L2, or ✕ | LT, or A | Space or Shift |\n120\t| Showstopper (screen bomb) | R1, or ○ | RB, or B | E or Right click |\n121\t| Showboat (taunt for ratings) | L1, or △ | LB, or Y | Q |\n122\t| Pause / menu | Options | Menu | Esc or P |\n123\t| Menus: move / confirm / back | D-pad, L-stick / ✕ / ○ | D-pad / A / B | Arrows, WASD / Enter, Space / Esc, Backspace; mouse hover focuses, click picks, wheel scrolls |\n124\t\n125\tThe face buttons are alternates for players who don't use the right stick. While twin-sticking, the thumbs are on the\n126\tsticks, so every combat action is on a shoulder or trigger. All actions can be rebound on the engine's standard Controls\n127\tscreen.\n128\t\n129\t### 4.2 Engine input presets\n130\t\n131\tDefine two presets and switch between them. Arrows must **aim** in play but **navigate** in menus. The engine keeps\n132\tarrows on the moves only if a preset lists them, so the play preset leaves them out.\n133\t\n134\t```js\n135\t// A preset lists every action it uses, the menu's own (start, pause, confirm, cancel) included.\n136\t// Mouse clicks in menus go through input.clicked() on the hovered item, not through 'confirm'.\n137\tconst MASH_MENU = { up: ['KeyW','ArrowUp','Pad12'], down: ['KeyS','ArrowDown','Pad13'], left: ['KeyA','ArrowLeft','Pad14'],\n138\t  right: ['KeyD','ArrowRight','Pad15'], start: ['Enter','NumpadEnter','Pad9'], pause: ['Escape','KeyP','Pad9'],\n139\t  confirm: ['Enter','NumpadEnter','Space','Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape','Backspace','Pad1'],\n140\t  tabL: ['KeyQ','Pad4'], tabR: ['KeyE','Pad5'], reset: ['KeyR','Pad3'] };          // tabs/reset: dev mode & pages\n141\tconst MASH_PLAY = { up: ['KeyW','Pad12'], down: ['KeyS','Pad13'], left: ['KeyA','Pad14'], right: ['KeyD','Pad15'],\n142\t  aimUp: ['ArrowUp'], aimDown: ['ArrowDown'], aimLeft: ['ArrowLeft'], aimRight: ['ArrowRight'],\n143\t  fire: ['Mouse0','Pad7'], slide: ['Space','ShiftLeft','ShiftRight','Pad6','Pad0'],\n144\t  bomb: ['KeyE','Mouse2','Pad5','Pad1'], showboat: ['KeyQ','Pad4','Pad3'],\n145\t  start: ['Enter','NumpadEnter','Pad9'], pause: ['Escape','KeyP','Pad9'],\n146\t  confirm: ['Enter','NumpadEnter','Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape','Backspace','Pad1'] };\n147\t```\n148\t\n149\t- Set `input: MASH_MENU` on front-end scenes and `input: MASH_PLAY` on play scenes (the scene's `input` field).\n150\t- **Preset sync hook (engine patch P1, §15.5).** While the pause menu (the Shell) or one of our overlays is open in play,\n151\t  every player's input must use `MASH_MENU`, so arrows move the focus. Expose the engine's internal `HOOKS` as `E.HOOKS`\n152\t  and push an input hook. The hook runs after `input.tick` and before the Shell reads navigation. It calls\n153\t  `p.use(want)` on each of `game.players` when the wanted preset changes: `MENU` if `game.paused || MT.overlay.open`,\n154\t  else the scene's preset. Changing presets calls `clear()`, which is fine at those moments.\n155\t- Joined players (`game.addPlayer`) copy P1's preset when they join. The hook keeps them in sync afterwards.\n156\t- Name the actions on the Controls screen with `menu.controls`: `{ fire: 'Fire', slide: 'Slide', bomb: 'Showstopper',\n157\t  showboat: 'Showboat', aimUp: 'Fire up (keyboard)', … , tabL: false, tabR: false, reset: false }`.\n158\t\n159\t### 4.3 How a contestant reads its intent each step\n160\t\n161\t`intentFrom(input, contestant)` returns `{ move:[x,y], aim: angle|null, fire: bool, slide: bool(pressed), bomb:\n162\tbool(pressed), showboat: bool(pressed) }`:\n163\t\n164\t1. **Move:** `input.move()` is in screen directions. Convert it with `game.view.screenDirToGround(mx, my)`.\n165\t2. **Aim**, in priority order:\n166\t   - The right stick, `input.padAim` (non-null past the dead zone; length > 0.35). Aim = the stick's screen direction\n167\t     converted to ground. Fire is true if Auto-fire is on (the default).\n168\t   - Arrow keys held: an 8-way direction from `aimUp/Down/Left/Right`. Fire is true.\n169\t   - The mouse, when `input.lastDevice === 'mouse'` or the mouse moved within the last 2 s. Aim = the angle from the\n170\t     contestant to `game.mouseGround()`. Fire = `down('fire')` (Left click).\n171\t   - Otherwise keep the last aim. `down('fire')` (R2) fires along it; if there's no aim yet, use the facing.\n172\t3. **Aim assist** (Settings, on by default for pads only): if an enemy is within 170 units and within ±10° of the aim,\n173\t   rotate the aim halfway toward it.\n174\t4. **Facing** follows the aim while firing; otherwise it follows movement.\n175\t\n176\tBots (attract mode, tests, the dev \"bot partner\") and remote players (§14) produce the same intent object. A contestant\n177\tnever reads an `E.Input` directly.\n178\t\n179\t### 4.4 Prompts and glyphs\n180\t\n181\t- Prompts follow `input.lastDevice`. On `gamepad`, show the button glyph in the family from the setting `glyphs`. On\n182\t  `keyboard`/`mouse`, show the keycap or mouse icon for that device's binding. Find the code with\n183\t  `input.map[action]` (first `Pad…` for pads; first key or `Mouse…` for keyboard and mouse); `input.codeLabel(code)`\n184\t  gives the text.\n185\t- **The 5×7 font has no ✕ ○ □ △.** Build `src/02-glyphs.js`: small pixel icons, 11×11 at scale 1, drawn with `E.px`.\n186\t  - PlayStation: ✕ blue `#7aa8ff`, ○ red `#ff6a6a`, □ pink `#ff8ad8` and △ green `#5fe0a0`, each on a dark disc. L1, R1,\n187\t    L2 and R2 are rounded tabs. Options and Create are pills; the sticks are L/R ringed discs; plus a D-pad cross.\n188\t  - Xbox: A green, B red, X blue and Y yellow letter discs; LB, RB, LT, RT, Menu and View.\n189\t  - Keyboard: a keycap with the label (1–6 chars; wide caps for Space, Shift, Enter and Esc).\n190\t  - Mouse: a mouse body with the left or right half lit.\n191\t\n192\t  API: `MT.glyph.draw(g, x, y, action, input, { scale })` returns the width it drew;\n193\t  `MT.glyph.prompt(g, x, y, [[action, 'TEXT'], …], input)` draws a row of icons with labels.\n194\t- **Engine patch P2:** the standard `glyphs` setting defaults to `'playstation'`, its options are\n195\t  `[['playstation','PlayStation'],['xbox','Xbox']]`, and its `apply` sets `glyphs` on **every** `game.players` input. A\n196\t  player who joins later inherits it.\n197\t\n198\t---\n199\t\n200\t## 5. Systems and mechanics\n201\t\n202\tAll numbers below are defaults. Every one marked **(T)** is a live tuning value with a dev slider (§13). Logic always reads\n203\t`MT.T.<key>` and never a literal.\n204\t\n205\t### 5.1 Contestants (the players)\n206\t\n207\t- **Body:** `new E.Body({ x, y, r: 6 })`. Speed `playerSpeed` **(T)** 95 u/s (×1.45 with Speed Sneakers), analog,\n208\t  colliding with the arena's walls, closed doors and solid props.\n209\t- **Rig:** `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.1, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'gun', … })`, dressed per look (§9.3). Each step:\n210\t  `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, point: aiming, hurt: hurtT > 0, flip: slideU, pose, expr })`. **Game\n211\t  logic never reads rig joints:** the muzzle is `x + cos(aim) * 10, y + sin(aim) * 10, z 14`.\n212\t- **HP and lives by difficulty:**\n213\t  - ROOKIE: HP 5, lives 5, enemy speed ×0.85, enemy bullets ×0.8.\n214\t  - CONTESTANT (default): HP 3, lives 3.\n215\t  - CHAMPION: HP 1, lives 3, enemy speed ×1.15. This is the classic one-hit rule.\n216\t\n217\t  Extra life at $250,000, $750,000, $1,500,000 and $3,000,000 per contestant, with an \"ENCORE!\" banner and the `oneup` sfx.\n218\t- **Getting hit** (no i-frames active): −1 HP (−2 from a brute charge or a boss slam).\n219\t  - 1.2 s invulnerability (`invulnTime` **(T)**), blinking at 12 Hz.\n220\t  - Knockback 120, `game.hitFx` (small), `input.rumble(.5, .15)`, ratings −12, a \"wrong answer\" buzzer and the crowd's \"OOOH\".\n221\t- **Death (HP 0):**\n222\t  - A \"MASHED!\" pop-up, a confetti burst in the player's colour, `pose: 'die'` then `down: 1`, and a Lance quip.\n223\t  - −1 life. The weapon and add-ons reset.\n224\t  - 2.0 s later the contestant **drops in on a cable** from the ceiling, under a spotlight near the entry door: z 70 → 0\n225\t    over 0.5 s. It has 2.5 s invulnerability and at least 1 Showstopper.\n226\t- **Out of lives (co-op):** state `out`, HUD \"OUT — PRESS START TO CONTINUE\".\n227\t  - Pressing Start (Options/Enter) brings the contestant back with full lives and **half their winnings** (the producer's\n228\t    cut). The run keeps going for the others.\n229\t  - When **every** contestant is out at once, the global CONTINUE countdown runs (§5.10).\n230\t- **Slide** (`slide`, pressed): 0.28 s at `slideSpeed` **(T)** 235 u/s in the move direction (or the facing if standing).\n231\t  - I-frames for the first 0.22 s. It can fire while sliding.\n232\t  - Cooldown `slideCooldown` **(T)** 0.85 s. Dust puff and a whoosh.\n233\t  - The rig rolls: pass `flip: u` (0→1 over the slide).\n234\t- **Showstopper** (`bomb`, pressed, stock > 0; max 3; 2 at the start of a run):\n235\t  - A 0.12 s white `game.flash` (it follows the comfort settings), a camera-flashbulb burst sound and a boom.\n236\t  - Ring particles and `particles.glints` everywhere.\n237\t  - Every enemy on screen takes 25 damage; boss parts take 30. All foe bullets are cleared, and enemies are stunned for 1.0 s.\n238\t  - Ratings +8. A 0.08 s `game.freeze` (not in sessions).\n239\t- **Showboat** (`showboat`, pressed, 3 s cooldown): a 0.6 s pose. Cycle `pose: 'cheer' | 'hips' | 'wave'` with\n240\t  `expr: 'smile'`; no moving or firing.\n241\t  - When it completes, let n = enemies within 64 units and m = enemies within 32. Ratings gain\n242\t    `4 + 3n + 3m` (cap 30), and a pop-up \"STYLE +N\".\n243\t  - Crowd cheer, louder with the gain. A hit during the pose cancels the gain.\n244\t  - This is how the show's theme becomes a risk/reward mechanic.\n245\t- **Walk-in:** at room `ENTER`, contestants walk from the entry door to a 2×2 formation 40 units inside. They are\n246\t  invulnerable and ignore input for 1.2 s.\n247\t- **Local drop-in:** `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, keys: false, onJoin })` stays open on every play scene. A joining pad gets\n248\t  the next free slot, colour and look, $0, default lives, and drops in on a cable.\n249\t\n250\t### 5.2 Weapons and power-ups\n251\t\n252\t| id | On-screen name | Kind | Behaviour | Duration (T: `puDuration` ×) |\n253\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n254\t| `blaster` | STUDIO BLASTER | primary (default) | 9 shots/s (`fireRate` T), bolt dmg 1 (`dmgMul` T), speed 330 (`bulletSpeed` T), r 2.5, life 0.9 s | ∞ |\n255\t| `spread` | TRIPLE PLAY | primary | 8/s, 3 bolts at −13°/0°/+13°, dmg 1 each | 14 s |\n256\t| `rockets` | PRIME-TIME ROCKETS | primary | 3.5/s, a rocket accelerating 180→300, direct dmg 4 + splash 3 (r 24), smoke trail, explodes on a hit, a wall or end of life (0.9 s) | 12 s |\n257\t| `popcorn` | POPCORN POPPER | primary | 2.5/s, a lobbed bag (`E.arc`) landing 90 ahead (or at the reticle if closer), splash 2 (r 18) + 6 kernels outward (dmg 1.5, speed 200, life 0.35, pierce 1). Clears crowds behind cover. | 12 s |\n258\t| `laser` | LIMELIGHT LASER | primary | a continuous beam from the muzzle to the first wall, piercing every enemy on the line, 16 DPS (`16*dt` per step), turn rate limited to 7 rad/s, a hum loop | 10 s |\n259\t| `records` | GOLD RECORDS | add-on | 2 gold discs orbit at r 26, 4.2 rad/s; each touch does 2 dmg (0.15 s cooldown per enemy) and destroys small foe bullets (orb, shard, coin, card, static) | 15 s |\n260\t| `shield` | SPONSOR SHIELD | add-on | invulnerable bubble with a flickering \"KRUNCH-O\" logo; touching enemies take 1 dmg per 0.2 s | 8 s |\n261\t| `speed` | SPEED SNEAKERS | add-on | move ×1.45, slide cooldown ×0.6, afterimages (`r.actor(..., { ghost })`) | 10 s |\n262\t| `bomb` | SHOWSTOPPER | instant | +1 stock (at max 3: +$2,000 instead) | — |\n263\t| `life` | ENCORE | instant | +1 life | — |\n264\t\n265\t- One **primary** slot. A new primary replaces the old one; the same primary refreshes its timer. Add-ons stack with the\n266\t  primary and with each other.\n267\t- In the HUD, the weapon icon has a draining bar. The last 2 s blink with a tick. At expiry a small \"BACK TO BASICS\".\n268\t- **Projectile tech:**\n269\t  - Blaster and spread bolts, the kernels and every foe bullet: `E.Bullets` pools on the `'ground'` plane, `pShots`\n270\t    (team `p`, `data: { owner, w }`) and `fShots` (team `f`, `data: { id, kind }`; ids are needed for netplay).\n271\t  - Rockets and popcorn bags are small custom projectile lists (update, draw and explode).\n272\t  - The laser is a per-step segment test against enemy circles; its length comes from stepping the ray against\n273\t    `map.heightAt` (or `map.ray`).\n274\t- Player bullets stop at walls and closed doors (`shots.update(dt, map)`).\n275\t\n276\t### 5.3 Pickups and economy\n277\t\n278\t| Pickup | Look (string sprite, ~10 px, bobbing, glow) | Effect |\n279\t|---|---|---|\n280\t| Bill | green banknote | $100 |\n281\t| Stack | banded stack | $500 |\n282\t| Gold bar | gold ingot with glint | $1,000 |\n283\t| Briefcase | silver case with \"$\" | $5,000 |\n284\t| Prize box | gift box (red, blue or gold, with a bow) | a named prize from the episode's table (§7.6), worth its value |\n285\t| Golden Key | gold key, star glint | team key +1 (out of 9) |\n286\t| Capsule | a mini CRT TV whose screen shows the power-up icon and its letter (S spread, R rockets, P popcorn, L laser, G gold records, B shield bubble, F fast sneakers) | the power-up |\n287\t| Showstopper | a flashbulb | +1 bomb |\n288\t| Encore | a gold star with \"1UP\" | +1 life |\n289\t| Golden Statuette | a big gold \"LANCIE\" award statue | Green Room grand prize (ends the bonus) |\n290\t\n291\t- **Collection:** a contestant touches it (radius = contestant r + 7).\n292\t  - Cash and prizes are credited × the ratings multiplier × `cashMul` **(T)**, to the collector only.\n293\t  - A pop-up \"+$1,500\" in the collector's colour, plus \"ka-ching\".\n294\t- **Lifetime:** 9 s on the floor, blinking for the last 2.5 s. Keys, placed items and the statuette never expire.\n295\t- **Magnet:** once a room is clear, cash within 60 units drifts to the nearest contestant.\n296\t- **Prize box:**\n297\t  - Draws the next prize from the episode table, shuffled with the run's seed, no repeats until it runs out.\n298\t  - A banner: \"YOU WON: A SELF-AWARE TOASTER! ($2,500)\", with Penny's squeal (babble).\n299\t  - The prize joins that player's recap list.\n300\t- **Keys** are shared by the team. A banner \"GOLDEN KEY 4/9\" and a chime; Lance's key line the first time."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eec69157-3f75-40b4-be93-e6ea9b3a321a","uuid":"dbb26f30-8b82-4808-9f12-56250e0025d6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:13.951Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050305__x4339a3/work/PLAN.md","content":"# MASH TV\n\n*A playful riff on Smash TV. I brainstormed fifty riffs on the source's name and numbered them, then drew one with Python's\n`secrets.randbelow(50) + 1`. It came up 9: **MASH TV**. Don't re-pick the title.*\n\n**Pitch.** MASH TV is a 1–4 player twin-stick arena shooter set inside the deadliest game show on television. Contestants\nfight through single-screen studio rooms while goons, robots and worse pour in through four doors. They grab cash and\nridiculous prizes, play to the cameras to keep the **ratings** up, and pick a route through the studio map. The goal is to\nsurvive three episodes, each capped by a giant boss, and reach the Season Finale. Collect enough Golden Keys and the\nsecret **Green Room** opens at the end. Your host is the immortal, oily, sequinned **Lance Lustre**: *\"KA-CHING! KA-BOOM!\"*\n\n**Names and files** (use the model id and timestamp from *your* TASK.md):\n\n| What | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Title on screen | `MASH TV` (sub-line: `LIVE FROM STUDIO 9`) |\n| GameTitle in file names | `MashTV` |\n| SOURCE in file names | `SmashTV` |\n| Dev folder (all dev files) | `MashTV-SmashTV-<model>-<timestamp>/` |\n| Deliverable (root, beside TASK.md) | `MashTV-SmashTV-<model>-<timestamp>.html` |\n| Exit interview (root, beside the HTML) | `exit-interview.json` |\n| \"Plan\" field in Source Information | `PLAN.md` |\n\n---\n\n## 0. Quick facts\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Genre | Twin-stick arena shooter (arcade). Co-op for 1–4 players, with a route choice between rooms. |\n| Perspective | One fixed single-screen arena per room, seen from a high three-quarter \"studio camera\": the engine view `threequarter` (pitch 55). `topdown` (pitch 80) is a Settings option. |\n| Engine | my-3D2dge handoff package **v0.85.2** (`github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge`, `dist/handoff/`; commit `4390a98` when planned). Use the full edition, `my-3d2dge.js`, which includes every module (we use `arcade`). |\n| Online | AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client `aihub-session 1.4.0`, **mode `shared-world`**, 1–4 players. |\n| Local multiplayer | 1–4 players on one screen: P1 on keyboard+mouse or a pad, P2–P4 on pads (drop-in with Options/Start). |\n| Length | A full run takes about 20–25 minutes: three episodes of 2–4 rooms plus a boss, then the bonus Green Room. A hub session round takes about 5–6 minutes. |\n| Output | One self-contained HTML file with the engine, the hub client and the game inlined. No image or audio files; everything is drawn and synthesized in code. |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Ground rules for the builder\n\n1. **TASK.md is the contract; this plan is how to meet it.** Where they disagree, TASK.md wins.\n2. **Work only inside your dev folder.** Other agents share the parent directories, ports and processes. Read nothing\n   outside your folder except what you fetch:\n   - Engine: shallow-clone it **inside your dev folder** (e.g. `.cache/my-3d2dge`; when this plan was written, `/tmp` on this\n     machine was a full tmpfs) with `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge .cache/my-3d2dge`.\n     Copy `dist/handoff/*` into the dev folder: the engine, the docs, the tools, the kits and `src/assets`.\n   - Hub: **don't clone ai-hub** (it's over 1 GB). Fetch the four files you need:\n     `curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/{session.js,harness.html,bridge.js,round.js}`\n     into `vendor/hub/`. `lib/hub/README.md` is the protocol; read it once, whole.\n3. **Servers and processes.** Prefer `file://` and headless Node. The hub harness needs a server: bind `127.0.0.1` on port 0\n   (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints the port, or a Node `http` server on port 0). Before trusting a\n   result, check that the page is your game (`window.MT` exists and the title is `MASH TV`). Stop only processes you\n   started, by PID. Never use `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\n4. **Read the engine docs before writing code.** Read `API.md` whole. Read `docs/ASSETS.md` whole before drawing props.\n   Grep `API-INDEX.md` for names; read the `AI_GUIDE.md` sections on Standard features, Frame order, Players, Testing\n   and the Twin-stick recipe. Every API name in this plan was checked against v0.85.2. If your copy is newer, grep the index.\n5. **Engine patches are allowed but kept small**, each listed with its reason in `engine/PATCHES.md`. That list feeds the\n   Engine Feedback. The patches this plan needs are in §15.5.\n6. **No TODOs, placeholders, stubs or \"coming soon\" anywhere.** Every menu item works; every feature in this plan ships.\n7. **One test command** (`npm test` → `node tools/test.mjs`) prints only failures and a one-line count. Rerun only the\n   suites whose code you changed (`--only <suite>`), and run everything before you hand off. Use screenshots only for\n   what a script can't check (§17.3). As TASK.md says, don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or\n   audit.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What makes Smash TV distinctive, and how MASH TV makes it play\n\n| Source trait | MASH TV mechanic or feature |\n|---|---|\n| A lethal TV game show played as entertainment, with a smarmy host | **Lance Lustre** reacts to everything on a **jumbotron** above the arena, with a lower-third subtitle and gibberish voice. The **Ratings** system turns \"be entertaining\" into a mechanic: it drives a cash multiplier, Prime Time, and producer \"stunts\" when you dawdle. |\n| Hordes flooding in through four doors | Door-spawn wave director: each door opens, enemies pour through and the door slams shut. Up to ~60 enemies on screen. |\n| Two-stick 8-way shooting while moving | Analog twin-stick (pad), mouse aim (PC), and 8-way arrow-key fire (keyboard only). |\n| Power-ups, cash and absurd consumer prizes | Timed weapons, cash × the ratings multiplier, and named joke prizes (\"A SELF-AWARE TOASTER\"). Co-host **Penny Prize** tallies them in a Prize Recap after each episode. |\n| A room-to-room map with path choice | Episode maps (3×3 grid). After a clear, the exits light up with the destination's name; walk through one to choose. Longer paths hold keys and cash; shorter paths carry less risk. |\n| Giant, multi-part bosses | **Mashy** the mascot (shoot off its parts), the **Wheel of Misfortune** (each spin picks the attack), **Lance in the Starmaker 9000**, then **The Network** itself. |\n| A secret bonus for collectors | **Golden Keys** (9 in the game). With 5 or more after the finale, you reach the **Green Room** and the true ending. |\n| Simultaneous co-op | 1–4 players in one arena, locally or online (AI Hub shared world). Ratings and keys are shared; cash is individual. |\n\n**Tone:** loud, garish and cartoon-violent. Enemies burst into **confetti, sparks and smoke** (no blood: \"BY ORDER OF THE\nFCC, ALL GORE HAS BEEN REPLACED WITH CONFETTI!\"). It's consumerist satire with a retro-future TV aesthetic: neon, chrome,\nmarquee bulbs, sponsor logos. **Writing style:** short, shouted, ALL-CAPS announcer lines with punchlines and fake sponsor\nplugs, like the source's barker energy. Every line is original (§8).\n\n---\n\n## 3. The game at a glance\n\n**Core loop (one sentence):** enter a sealed studio room, survive the waves pouring from its doors while grabbing cash,\nprizes and power-ups, then pick the next door on the studio map, until you reach and beat the episode's boss.\n\n**Flow:**\n\n```\nBoot ─► Title ─(10 s idle)─► Attract demo ─(any input)─► Title\nTitle menu: START THE SHOW · EPISODES · HOW TO PLAY · TOP EARNERS · OPTIONS · ABOUT & CREDITS\nSTART THE SHOW ─► Difficulty ─► Contestant Lobby (join 1–4) ─► Cold Open ─► Episode 1 card\n  ─► Room ─► (clear) ─► choose exit ─► \"NEXT ON MASH TV\" map card ─► Room … ─► Boss ─► Prize Recap\n  ─► Episode 2 card … Boss ─► Prize Recap ─► Episode 3 card … Finale (Lance ─► The Network) ─► Prize Recap\n  ─► keys ≥ 5 ? Green Room ─► Ending B (true ending) : Ending A\n  ─► Initials (each qualifying player) ─► Top Earners ─► Title\nAll lives lost (every player out) ─► CONTINUE? 10…0 (✕/Enter: continue, −50 % winnings) ─► else Game Over ─► Initials ─► Top Earners ─► Title\nAI Hub session: Our own card (contestant line-up) ─► 3-2-1 ─► Lightning Round (3 rooms + Mashy) ─► finish ─► end card\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Controls and input\n\n### 4.1 Bindings\n\n| Action | DualSense (default glyphs) | Xbox glyphs (Settings) | Keyboard + mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Move | L-stick, D-pad | L-stick, D-pad | W A S D |\n| Aim + fire | R-stick (fires while pushed past 0.35) | R-stick | Mouse aims (reticle); **hold Left click** fires |\n| Fire (in the last aim direction) | R2 (hold) | RT | — |\n| 8-way fire (keyboard only) | — | — | Arrow keys (hold; two arrows = diagonal) |\n| Slide (dodge with i-frames) | L2, or ✕ | LT, or A | Space or Shift |\n| Showstopper (screen bomb) | R1, or ○ | RB, or B | E or Right click |\n| Showboat (taunt for ratings) | L1, or △ | LB, or Y | Q |\n| Pause / menu | Options | Menu | Esc or P |\n| Menus: move / confirm / back | D-pad, L-stick / ✕ / ○ | D-pad / A / B | Arrows, WASD / Enter, Space / Esc, Backspace; mouse hover focuses, click picks, wheel scrolls |\n\nThe face buttons are alternates for players who don't use the right stick. While twin-sticking, the thumbs are on the\nsticks, so every combat action is on a shoulder or trigger. All actions can be rebound on the engine's standard Controls\nscreen.\n\n### 4.2 Engine input presets\n\nDefine two presets and switch between them. Arrows must **aim** in play but **navigate** in menus. The engine keeps\narrows on the moves only if a preset lists them, so the play preset leaves them out.\n\n```js\n// A preset lists every action it uses, the menu's own (start, pause, confirm, cancel) included.\n// Mouse clicks in menus go through input.clicked() on the hovered item, not through 'confirm'.\nconst MASH_MENU = { up: ['KeyW','ArrowUp','Pad12'], down: ['KeyS','ArrowDown','Pad13'], left: ['KeyA','ArrowLeft','Pad14'],\n  right: ['KeyD','ArrowRight','Pad15'], start: ['Enter','NumpadEnter','Pad9'], pause: ['Escape','KeyP','Pad9'],\n  confirm: ['Enter','NumpadEnter','Space','Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape','Backspace','Pad1'],\n  tabL: ['KeyQ','Pad4'], tabR: ['KeyE','Pad5'], reset: ['KeyR','Pad3'] };          // tabs/reset: dev mode & pages\nconst MASH_PLAY = { up: ['KeyW','Pad12'], down: ['KeyS','Pad13'], left: ['KeyA','Pad14'], right: ['KeyD','Pad15'],\n  aimUp: ['ArrowUp'], aimDown: ['ArrowDown'], aimLeft: ['ArrowLeft'], aimRight: ['ArrowRight'],\n  fire: ['Mouse0','Pad7'], slide: ['Space','ShiftLeft','ShiftRight','Pad6','Pad0'],\n  bomb: ['KeyE','Mouse2','Pad5','Pad1'], showboat: ['KeyQ','Pad4','Pad3'],\n  start: ['Enter','NumpadEnter','Pad9'], pause: ['Escape','KeyP','Pad9'],\n  confirm: ['Enter','NumpadEnter','Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape','Backspace','Pad1'] };\n```\n\n- Set `input: MASH_MENU` on front-end scenes and `input: MASH_PLAY` on play scenes (the scene's `input` field).\n- **Preset sync hook (engine patch P1, §15.5).** While the pause menu (the Shell) or one of our overlays is open in play,\n  every player's input must use `MASH_MENU`, so arrows move the focus. Expose the engine's internal `HOOKS` as `E.HOOKS`\n  and push an input hook. The hook runs after `input.tick` and before the Shell reads navigation. It calls\n  `p.use(want)` on each of `game.players` when the wanted preset changes: `MENU` if `game.paused || MT.overlay.open`,\n  else the scene's preset. Changing presets calls `clear()`, which is fine at those moments.\n- Joined players (`game.addPlayer`) copy P1's preset when they join. The hook keeps them in sync afterwards.\n- Name the actions on the Controls screen with `menu.controls`: `{ fire: 'Fire', slide: 'Slide', bomb: 'Showstopper',\n  showboat: 'Showboat', aimUp: 'Fire up (keyboard)', … , tabL: false, tabR: false, reset: false }`.\n\n### 4.3 How a contestant reads its intent each step\n\n`intentFrom(input, contestant)` returns `{ move:[x,y], aim: angle|null, fire: bool, slide: bool(pressed), bomb:\nbool(pressed), showboat: bool(pressed) }`:\n\n1. **Move:** `input.move()` is in screen directions. Convert it with `game.view.screenDirToGround(mx, my)`.\n2. **Aim**, in priority order:\n   - The right stick, `input.padAim` (non-null past the dead zone; length > 0.35). Aim = the stick's screen direction\n     converted to ground. Fire is true if Auto-fire is on (the default).\n   - Arrow keys held: an 8-way direction from `aimUp/Down/Left/Right`. Fire is true.\n   - The mouse, when `input.lastDevice === 'mouse'` or the mouse moved within the last 2 s. Aim = the angle from the\n     contestant to `game.mouseGround()`. Fire = `down('fire')` (Left click).\n   - Otherwise keep the last aim. `down('fire')` (R2) fires along it; if there's no aim yet, use the facing.\n3. **Aim assist** (Settings, on by default for pads only): if an enemy is within 170 units and within ±10° of the aim,\n   rotate the aim halfway toward it.\n4. **Facing** follows the aim while firing; otherwise it follows movement.\n\nBots (attract mode, tests, the dev \"bot partner\") and remote players (§14) produce the same intent object. A contestant\nnever reads an `E.Input` directly.\n\n### 4.4 Prompts and glyphs\n\n- Prompts follow `input.lastDevice`. On `gamepad`, show the button glyph in the family from the setting `glyphs`. On\n  `keyboard`/`mouse`, show the keycap or mouse icon for that device's binding. Find the code with\n  `input.map[action]` (first `Pad…` for pads; first key or `Mouse…` for keyboard and mouse); `input.codeLabel(code)`\n  gives the text.\n- **The 5×7 font has no ✕ ○ □ △.** Build `src/02-glyphs.js`: small pixel icons, 11×11 at scale 1, drawn with `E.px`.\n  - PlayStation: ✕ blue `#7aa8ff`, ○ red `#ff6a6a`, □ pink `#ff8ad8` and △ green `#5fe0a0`, each on a dark disc. L1, R1,\n    L2 and R2 are rounded tabs. Options and Create are pills; the sticks are L/R ringed discs; plus a D-pad cross.\n  - Xbox: A green, B red, X blue and Y yellow letter discs; LB, RB, LT, RT, Menu and View.\n  - Keyboard: a keycap with the label (1–6 chars; wide caps for Space, Shift, Enter and Esc).\n  - Mouse: a mouse body with the left or right half lit.\n\n  API: `MT.glyph.draw(g, x, y, action, input, { scale })` returns the width it drew;\n  `MT.glyph.prompt(g, x, y, [[action, 'TEXT'], …], input)` draws a row of icons with labels.\n- **Engine patch P2:** the standard `glyphs` setting defaults to `'playstation'`, its options are\n  `[['playstation','PlayStation'],['xbox','Xbox']]`, and its `apply` sets `glyphs` on **every** `game.players` input. A\n  player who joins later inherits it.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Systems and mechanics\n\nAll numbers below are defaults. Every one marked **(T)** is a live tuning value with a dev slider (§13). Logic always reads\n`MT.T.<key>` and never a literal.\n\n### 5.1 Contestants (the players)\n\n- **Body:** `new E.Body({ x, y, r: 6 })`. Speed `playerSpeed` **(T)** 95 u/s (×1.45 with Speed Sneakers), analog,\n  colliding with the arena's walls, closed doors and solid props.\n- **Rig:** `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.1, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'gun', … })`, dressed per look (§9.3). Each step:\n  `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, point: aiming, hurt: hurtT > 0, flip: slideU, pose, expr })`. **Game\n  logic never reads rig joints:** the muzzle is `x + cos(aim) * 10, y + sin(aim) * 10, z 14`.\n- **HP and lives by difficulty:**\n  - ROOKIE: HP 5, lives 5, enemy speed ×0.85, enemy bullets ×0.8.\n  - CONTESTANT (default): HP 3, lives 3.\n  - CHAMPION: HP 1, lives 3, enemy speed ×1.15. This is the classic one-hit rule.\n\n  Extra life at $250,000, $750,000, $1,500,000 and $3,000,000 per contestant, with an \"ENCORE!\" banner and the `oneup` sfx.\n- **Getting hit** (no i-frames active): −1 HP (−2 from a brute charge or a boss slam).\n  - 1.2 s invulnerability (`invulnTime` **(T)**), blinking at 12 Hz.\n  - Knockback 120, `game.hitFx` (small), `input.rumble(.5, .15)`, ratings −12, a \"wrong answer\" buzzer and the crowd's \"OOOH\".\n- **Death (HP 0):**\n  - A \"MASHED!\" pop-up, a confetti burst in the player's colour, `pose: 'die'` then `down: 1`, and a Lance quip.\n  - −1 life. The weapon and add-ons reset.\n  - 2.0 s later the contestant **drops in on a cable** from the ceiling, under a spotlight near the entry door: z 70 → 0\n    over 0.5 s. It has 2.5 s invulnerability and at least 1 Showstopper.\n- **Out of lives (co-op):** state `out`, HUD \"OUT — PRESS START TO CONTINUE\".\n  - Pressing Start (Options/Enter) brings the contestant back with full lives and **half their winnings** (the producer's\n    cut). The run keeps going for the others.\n  - When **every** contestant is out at once, the global CONTINUE countdown runs (§5.10).\n- **Slide** (`slide`, pressed): 0.28 s at `slideSpeed` **(T)** 235 u/s in the move direction (or the facing if standing).\n  - I-frames for the first 0.22 s. It can fire while sliding.\n  - Cooldown `slideCooldown` **(T)** 0.85 s. Dust puff and a whoosh.\n  - The rig rolls: pass `flip: u` (0→1 over the slide).\n- **Showstopper** (`bomb`, pressed, stock > 0; max 3; 2 at the start of a run):\n  - A 0.12 s white `game.flash` (it follows the comfort settings), a camera-flashbulb burst sound and a boom.\n  - Ring particles and `particles.glints` everywhere.\n  - Every enemy on screen takes 25 damage; boss parts take 30. All foe bullets are cleared, and enemies are stunned for 1.0 s.\n  - Ratings +8. A 0.08 s `game.freeze` (not in sessions).\n- **Showboat** (`showboat`, pressed, 3 s cooldown): a 0.6 s pose. Cycle `pose: 'cheer' | 'hips' | 'wave'` with\n  `expr: 'smile'`; no moving or firing.\n  - When it completes, let n = enemies within 64 units and m = enemies within 32. Ratings gain\n    `4 + 3n + 3m` (cap 30), and a pop-up \"STYLE +N\".\n  - Crowd cheer, louder with the gain. A hit during the pose cancels the gain.\n  - This is how the show's theme becomes a risk/reward mechanic.\n- **Walk-in:** at room `ENTER`, contestants walk from the entry door to a 2×2 formation 40 units inside. They are\n  invulnerable and ignore input for 1.2 s.\n- **Local drop-in:** `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, keys: false, onJoin })` stays open on every play scene. A joining pad gets\n  the next free slot, colour and look, $0, default lives, and drops in on a cable.\n\n### 5.2 Weapons and power-ups\n\n| id | On-screen name | Kind | Behaviour | Duration (T: `puDuration` ×) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `blaster` | STUDIO BLASTER | primary (default) | 9 shots/s (`fireRate` T), bolt dmg 1 (`dmgMul` T), speed 330 (`bulletSpeed` T), r 2.5, life 0.9 s | ∞ |\n| `spread` | TRIPLE PLAY | primary | 8/s, 3 bolts at −13°/0°/+13°, dmg 1 each | 14 s |\n| `rockets` | PRIME-TIME ROCKETS | primary | 3.5/s, a rocket accelerating 180→300, direct dmg 4 + splash 3 (r 24), smoke trail, explodes on a hit, a wall or end of life (0.9 s) | 12 s |\n| `popcorn` | POPCORN POPPER | primary | 2.5/s, a lobbed bag (`E.arc`) landing 90 ahead (or at the reticle if closer), splash 2 (r 18) + 6 kernels outward (dmg 1.5, speed 200, life 0.35, pierce 1). Clears crowds behind cover. | 12 s |\n| `laser` | LIMELIGHT LASER | primary | a continuous beam from the muzzle to the first wall, piercing every enemy on the line, 16 DPS (`16*dt` per step), turn rate limited to 7 rad/s, a hum loop | 10 s |\n| `records` | GOLD RECORDS | add-on | 2 gold discs orbit at r 26, 4.2 rad/s; each touch does 2 dmg (0.15 s cooldown per enemy) and destroys small foe bullets (orb, shard, coin, card, static) | 15 s |\n| `shield` | SPONSOR SHIELD | add-on | invulnerable bubble with a flickering \"KRUNCH-O\" logo; touching enemies take 1 dmg per 0.2 s | 8 s |\n| `speed` | SPEED SNEAKERS | add-on | move ×1.45, slide cooldown ×0.6, afterimages (`r.actor(..., { ghost })`) | 10 s |\n| `bomb` | SHOWSTOPPER | instant | +1 stock (at max 3: +$2,000 instead) | — |\n| `life` | ENCORE | instant | +1 life | — |\n\n- One **primary** slot. A new primary replaces the old one; the same primary refreshes its timer. Add-ons stack with the\n  primary and with each other.\n- In the HUD, the weapon icon has a draining bar. The last 2 s blink with a tick. At expiry a small \"BACK TO BASICS\".\n- **Projectile tech:**\n  - Blaster and spread bolts, the kernels and every foe bullet: `E.Bullets` pools on the `'ground'` plane, `pShots`\n    (team `p`, `data: { owner, w }`) and `fShots` (team `f`, `data: { id, kind }`; ids are needed for netplay).\n  - Rockets and popcorn bags are small custom projectile lists (update, draw and explode).\n  - The laser is a per-step segment test against enemy circles; its length comes from stepping the ray against\n    `map.heightAt` (or `map.ray`).\n- Player bullets stop at walls and closed doors (`shots.update(dt, map)`).\n\n### 5.3 Pickups and economy\n\n| Pickup | Look (string sprite, ~10 px, bobbing, glow) | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bill | green banknote | $100 |\n| Stack | banded stack | $500 |\n| Gold bar | gold ingot with glint | $1,000 |\n| Briefcase | silver case with \"$\" | $5,000 |\n| Prize box | gift box (red, blue or gold, with a bow) | a named prize from the episode's table (§7.6), worth its value |\n| Golden Key | gold key, star glint | team key +1 (out of 9) |\n| Capsule | a mini CRT TV whose screen shows the power-up icon and its letter (S spread, R rockets, P popcorn, L laser, G gold records, B shield bubble, F fast sneakers) | the power-up |\n| Showstopper | a flashbulb | +1 bomb |\n| Encore | a gold star with \"1UP\" | +1 life |\n| Golden Statuette | a big gold \"LANCIE\" award statue | Green Room grand prize (ends the bonus) |\n\n- **Collection:** a contestant touches it (radius = contestant r + 7).\n  - Cash and prizes are credited × the ratings multiplier × `cashMul` **(T)**, to the collector only.\n  - A pop-up \"+$1,500\" in the collector's colour, plus \"ka-ching\".\n- **Lifetime:** 9 s on the floor, blinking for the last 2.5 s. Keys, placed items and the statuette never expire.\n- **Magnet:** once a room is clear, cash within 60 units drifts to the nearest contestant.\n- **Prize box:**\n  - Draws the next prize from the episode table, shuffled with the run's seed, no repeats until it runs out.\n  - A banner: \"YOU WON: A SELF-AWARE TOASTER! ($2,500)\", with Penny's squeal (babble).\n  - The prize joins that player's recap list.\n- **Keys** are shared by the team. A banner \"GOLDEN KEY 4/9\" and a chime; Lance's key line the first time.","numLines":300,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2017}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013FTyUAsoncSkwaKFhDMoR5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrY2MgEQ1nVHmhMujZW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QCgRDJC8HDS3DK9aJDzwhK","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050305__x4339a3/work/PLAN.md","offset":301,"limit":400},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10842,"cache_read_input_tokens":25896,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10842},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eec69157-3f75-40b4-be93-e6ea9b3a321a","uuid":"cd0ce8a1-e7ce-4bc6-b618-3820f4be14f1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:16.364Z","request_id":"req_011CghrY23L77nwKVAw981hz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QCgRDJC8HDS3DK9aJDzwhK":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050305__x4339a3/work/PLAN.md","offset":301,"limit":400}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCgRDJC8HDS3DK9aJDzwhK","type":"tool_result","content":"301\t- **Drops** on enemy death roll the enemy's drop table (§5.8) × `dropMul` **(T)**. Floor caps: at most 3 capsules and\n302\t  25 cash pickups at once.\n303\t- **Prize crates** are placed props: HP 3, solid while whole (`map.solid`, or a static body). When broken they spill\n304\t  3–5 cash, a 50 % chance of a prize, and the key if the room's data says so.\n305\t\n306\t### 5.4 Ratings (the show's heartbeat)\n307\t\n308\t- `R` runs 0–100 and is **shared by the team**: it's the show's rating, not a player's. It's drawn top-centre as a big TV\n309\t  \"RATINGS\" gauge with a needle, the multiplier and an APPLAUSE light.\n310\t- **Gains:**\n311\t  - A kill adds the enemy's `rat` value. A multi-kill adds +2 for each kill past 2 within 0.4 s.\n312\t  - Showboat (§5.1).\n313\t  - A **near miss**: +0.5 when a foe bullet passes within 7 units of a contestant without hitting (at most 3 a second).\n314\t  - A prize +2, a key +5, a boss part destroyed +10.\n315\t  - All gains × `ratingsGain` **(T)**.\n316\t- **Losses:** a hit −12; a death −25; BANKRUPT (the wheel) −10.\n317\t- **Decay:** after 2.5 s without a gain, R falls by `ratingsDecay` **(T)** 2.5 a second.\n318\t- **Multiplier:** R < 20 ×1; < 40 ×2; < 60 ×3; < 80 ×4; ≥ 80 ×5.\n319\t- **PRIME TIME** when R reaches 100. It lasts `primeTime` **(T)** 12 s:\n320\t  - The multiplier is locked at ×5.\n321\t  - A \"PRIME TIME!\" banner and fanfare sting; `audio.layer('prime', 1, .3)` brings the brass in.\n322\t  - The audience throws 3 random capsules in arcs from the bleachers; confetti cannons fire; the APPLAUSE sign blinks.\n323\t  - Afterwards R = 60, with a 20 s cooldown before the next Prime Time.\n324\t- **RATINGS STUNT** (anti-stall): if R < 5 for 10 s during waves, \"WE'RE LOSING VIEWERS!\" and the producers release the\n325\t  episode's stunt from a random door:\n326\t  - Ep1: 12 clapbots.\n327\t  - Ep2: a dolly tank.\n328\t  - Ep3: a mascot brute.\n329\t\n330\t  R +15. At most once per room.\n331\t\n332\t### 5.5 Arena, doors and hazards\n333\t\n334\t**Geometry, the same in every room.** A TileMap of 23 × 15 cells is 368 × 240 world units.\n335\t- **Walls:** row 0, row 14, col 0 and col 22, wall type 1: `h: 26`, studio-flat faces (§9.2).\n336\t  - The south wall row is `cut: true`, so it never hides the floor from the camera.\n337\t- **Interior:** 21 × 13 cells, x 16–352, y 16–224, centre **(184, 120)**.\n338\t- **Door gaps** (3 cells, wall type 2, painted by our door painter):\n339\t  - N: cols 10–12 of row 0. S: cols 10–12 of row 14. W: rows 6–8 of col 0. E: rows 6–8 of col 22.\n340\t  - Door centres: N (184, 8), S (184, 232), W (8, 120), E (360, 120).\n341\t- **Room data uses interior cells** `[cx, cy]`, cx 0–20 and cy 0–12. In world units that's\n342\t  `(24 + cx * 16, 24 + cy * 16)`.\n343\t\n344\t**Door states:**\n345\t- `closed`.\n346\t- `opening`: 0.35 s; the shutter rolls up, a red beacon and a klaxon.\n347\t- `open`: spawning.\n348\t- `closing`: 0.3 s; a slam and dust.\n349\t- `exit`: a green beacon and a lit sign above the door with the destination's name and room-type icon. Its cells become\n350\t  walkable (`map.set(cx, cy, 0)`), with an exit trigger 10 units past the threshold.\n351\t\n352\t**Spawning:**\n353\t- From a **door:** enemies appear 20 units outside the gap and walk in with wall collision off (\"entering\") until inside\n354\t  the interior. The door stays open while its queue has spawns, plus 0.6 s.\n355\t- From the **audience** (hecklers): a leap from the E or W bleachers over the wall. An arc from x −30 or 398 to a random\n356\t  interior point on that side; 0.7 s, invulnerable in the air.\n357\t- **Drop:** from the ceiling at a random free interior point at least 50 units from every contestant. A shadow\n358\t  telegraphs for 0.6 s, then it falls.\n359\t\n360\t**Hazards:**\n361\t- **Conveyor belts** (Ep2): strips 2 cells tall across the room. Each pushes everything on it (contestants, enemies,\n362\t  pickups, the key) at ±40 u/s, with animated chevrons. Direction reverses every 12 s after a 1.5 s warning (lights, an\n363\t  alarm, the belt slowing).\n364\t- **Pyro vents** (Ep3): floor grates firing in data-driven patterns.\n365\t  - Telegraph: 1.0 s of glow, sparks and rumble.\n366\t  - Then a 1.2 s flame column, r 12: 1 damage to contestants, 3 damage a second to enemies. It's emissive and casts light.\n367\t- **Tomato splats:** puddles of r 14 for 6 s that slow contestants to ×0.6.\n368\t- **Prize crates** and **vault locks:** static targets (rooms 1-6, 2-6, 3-4).\n369\t\n370\t**Camera:**\n371\t- Fixed: `game.focus(184, 120, 0)` every update.\n372\t- Zoom is fitted so the walled arena fills the screen, leaving ~22 px top and bottom for the HUD. Measure\n373\t  `map.bounds(game.view)` at zoom 1 and recompute when the screen changes size (`game.screen.listeners`). Clamp to\n374\t  [0.6, 1.6], then × `camZoom` **(T)**.\n375\t- The scene's `camera: { zoom: false }` turns the player's zoom off. Shake goes through `game.shake` (comfort settings\n376\t  apply).\n377\t- Wide or tall screens show the studio around the arena (bleachers, cranes, the jumbotron; §9.2).\n378\t\n379\t### 5.6 Room flow (phases)\n380\t\n381\t`ENTER` → `INTRO` → `WAVES` → `CLEAR` → `EXIT` → `TRANSITION` → the next room's `ENTER`.\n382\t\n383\t- **ENTER** (1.2 s): the walk-in. The door behind the contestants slams.\n384\t- **INTRO** (≤ 2 s): Lance's room line on the jumbotron and a \"MASH!\" stinger. An episode's first room is preceded by the\n385\t  episode card (§11.3).\n386\t- **WAVES:** the room script (§5.7) runs.\n387\t- **CLEAR:** every wave has spawned and no counted enemy is alive. Mimes, crates and vault locks don't count.\n388\t  - \"ROOM CLEAR!\" banner and sting.\n389\t  - Each living contestant gets a clear bonus of `$1,000 × episode × multiplier`, +50 % if cleared under the room's\n390\t    `par` seconds.\n391\t  - A Lance line. Remaining foe bullets fade out.\n392\t- **EXIT:** the exit doors open with their signs. The first contestant into an exit trigger picks it; 0.8 s later every\n393\t  contestant goes. Pickups can still be collected meanwhile.\n394\t  - If nobody leaves within 25 s: \"HURRY UP!\" and 4 clapbots every 6 s from the doors that aren't exits.\n395\t- **TRANSITION:** a 0.4 s TV-static wipe, then the \"NEXT ON MASH TV\" map card (2.5 s, skippable with confirm), then\n396\t  another static wipe into the next room.\n397\t\n398\t**Boss rooms:** `ENTER` → `BOSS_INTRO` (~4 s cutscene, skippable) → `BOSS` → `BOSS_DEATH` (3 s) → `CLEAR` → the `recap`\n399\tscene.\n400\t\n401\t**Survive rooms** (1-4): `WAVES` ends when the timer runs out and the field is clear.\n402\t\n403\t### 5.7 Waves: the room script data format\n404\t\n405\t```js\n406\t// src/20-content-*.js — one room\n407\t{ id: '1-2', name: 'MIME FIELD', ep: 1, type: 'battle', cell: [0, 2], exits: { N: '1-4' }, par: 60,\n408\t  place: [['mime', 4, 3], ['mime', 10, 2] /* … */],      // [kind, cx, cy] at room start (interior cells)\n409\t  items: [[1.5, 'spread', [5, 6]]],                      // [seconds after WAVES starts, pickup, 'center' | 'drop' | [cx, cy]]\n410\t  key: { rule: 'mimes' },                                 // 'mimes' | 'place' | 'crate' | 'carrier' | 'vault' | 'final' | 'survive'\n411\t  hazards: [],                                            // e.g. { kind: 'conveyor', rows: [3, 6, 9], dirs: [1, -1, 1] }\n412\t  waves: [\n413\t    { at: 2, spawn: [['S', 'goon', 8]] },\n414\t    { left: 3, at: 8, spawn: [['N', 'popper', 2], ['E', 'goon', 8]] },\n415\t    { left: 3, at: 10, spawn: [['W', 'goon', 10]], items: [['rockets', 'drop']] },\n416\t  ] }\n417\t```\n418\t\n419\t- **When a wave starts:** `at` seconds after the previous wave started, or when no more than `left` counted enemies are\n420\t  alive, whichever comes first. With only one of them given, that one alone. Build it as one `game.script` per room:\n421\t  `yield E.any([w.at, () => alive() <= w.left])`.\n422\t- **A spawn entry** is `[door, kind, n, gap = 0.25]`. Doors:\n423\t  - `N`, `E`, `S`, `W` for one door.\n424\t  - `all` (each door gets n), `sides` (E and W), `ends` (N and S).\n425\t  - `audience`, `drop`, or `[cx, cy]` for an exact cell.\n426\t- **Scaling:** `n' = round(n × (1 + 0.35 × (players − 1)) × waveSize (T) × difficulty)`, where difficulty is ROOKIE 0.8,\n427\t  CONTESTANT 1 or CHAMPION 1.2. Lower `spawnGap` **(T)** packs the spawns tighter.\n428\t- **The room ends** when the last wave has spawned and the field is clear. With `{ final: true, script: 'name' }` a wave\n429\t  runs a named scripted event (the Pyro Pit's FINALE BURST).\n430\t\n431\t### 5.8 Enemies\n432\t\n433\tAll enemies share an archetype record:\n434\t`{ kind, hp, speed, r, contact, cash, rat, drops, make(world, x, y, o), update(e, dt, world), draw(r, e) }`.\n435\t\n436\tEach draws from `e.rs`, a render state `{ x, y, z, face, vx, vy, state, t, hpPct, flash, alpha }`, so the same draw code\n437\tworks on hub clients (§14.3). Common rules:\n438\t- Target the nearest living contestant. Separate from each other with an `E.SpatialHash` (radius 10, a soft push), so\n439\t  crowds don't stack.\n440\t- Telegraph every attack with a visible wind-up of at least 0.3 s.\n441\t- On a hit, flash white (`r.actor(..., { flash })`) with a small knockback.\n442\t- On death, a confetti burst in the enemy's palette (`particles.bits`), a cash pop-up, a pop sound and the drop roll.\n443\t- `enemySpeed`, `enemyHp`, `enemyBulletSpeed` and `contactDmg` are **(T)** multipliers.\n444\t\n445\t| kind | HP | Speed | Behaviour | Telegraph | Cash / rat | Drops |\n446\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n447\t| `goon` (STUDIO SECURITY) | 1 | 52 ±6 | Walks straight at the target in loose flocks. Within 16 units, a baton swing (`E.Attack('bash')`, wind 0.3 s, reach 14). Contact dmg 1. | the baton rises (wind) | $100 / 1 | bill 8 %, capsule 1.2 %, prize 1 % |\n448\t| `clapbot` (APPLAUSE ROBOT) | 1 | hop 115 | Hops every 0.4 s toward the target ±40° (erratic). Clapper hands clap on each hop. Contact dmg 1. | squash before the hop | $150 / 1 | bill 10 % |\n449\t| `popper` (PARTY POPPER) | 2 | 38 | Waddles to the target. Within 18 units it lights its fuse (0.6 s: inflates, flashes, hisses), then bursts into a ring of 8 confetti shards (speed 90, life 1.2 s). It also bursts when killed. | swelling and a fuse spark | $250 / 2 | stack 10 %, capsule 3 % |\n450\t| `mime` (LAND MIME) | 1 | 0 | Stands still, half-visible (alpha 0.45), miming \"trapped in a box\". When a contestant is within 34 units: a 0.7 s telegraph (hands up, shaking, beeps), then a blast of r 36 (dmg 1). Shot first, it pops harmlessly. **Doesn't count for room clear.** | a beep and shaking | $300 / 2 | bill 30 % |\n451\t| `disco` (DISCO BALL) | 5 (big: 10) | 70 | Bounces diagonally off walls. Every 3 s, 4 light shots in a + or × pattern, alternating (speed 110). A **big** one splits into 2 small ones (HP 3) when it dies. Contact dmg 1. | facets flare 0.4 s | $400 (big $800) / 3 | stack 20 %, capsule 5 % |\n452\t| `heckler` (STUDIO AUDIENCE) | 3 | 45 | Arrives over the wall. Keeps 70–110 units from the target and strafes. Every 2.2 s lobs a rotten tomato (`E.arc` to where the target will be in 0.6 s); the splat does dmg 1 within r 10 and leaves a slow puddle. | a red ring on the floor where it lands, the throw pose (`E.MOVES.throw`) | $350 / 2 | prize 6 %, capsule 4 % |\n453\t| `tank` (DOLLY TANK) | 14 | 26 | A camera dolly turned tank. The chassis turns slowly; the camera-turret tracks the target at 1.4 rad/s. Every 2.4 s it fires a shell (speed 120) that explodes at walls or contestants (r 16, dmg 1). On death it explodes, damaging enemies too. | lens flash and an aim line, 0.4 s | $1,000 / 6 | case 15 %, capsule 15 % |\n454\t| `snake` (CABLE SNAKE) | head 8, segments 2 × 10 | 60 | A head plug and 10 cable segments that follow the head's path history (one point every 6 units). It weaves toward the target. Shot-off segments shorten it; segments can be hit independently. Contact dmg 1. | the head rears back before a 1.5× lunge | head $1,200 / 5, seg $150 / 1 | head: case 30 % |\n455\t| `brute` (THE CEREAL KILLER, a mascot) | 24 | walk 40, charge 220 | Walks at the target. Every 4 s: a 0.8 s telegraph (stomps, floor rings, a roar), then a straight charge of up to 1.4 s. Hitting a wall stuns it for 1.5 s, and stunned it takes ×2 damage. Contact dmg 2. | a stomp, rings on the floor, a red line along the charge | $2,000 / 8 | case 40 %, capsule 25 % |\n456\t| `hecklerKing` (2-4 only) | 12 | 45 | A heckler with a foam crown who throws 3-tomato volleys. Carries the room's key. | as heckler | $1,500 / 6 | key |\n457\t| `crate` | 3 | — | A static prize crate (see §5.3). | — | — | cash, prize, key |\n458\t| `lock` (3-4 only) | 15 | — | A vault bolt on the north wall; when all 4 break, the safe opens. | — | $500 / 2 | — |\n459\t\n460\tEnemy foe-bullet kinds, used across enemies and bosses:\n461\t- `orb` (generic): r 3.\n462\t- `shard` (confetti): r 2.\n463\t- `beam` (disco light): r 2, long.\n464\t- `tomato`: a lob with z.\n465\t- `shell`: explodes.\n466\t- `butter`, `gravy`, `coin`, `card` (spins), `static` (jittery), `tot` (lobbed, bursts into 6 shards).\n467\t\n468\tSpeeds stay at 70–130, readable at 10 feet, each with a bright core and a dark outline.\n469\t\n470\t### 5.9 Bosses\n471\t\n472\t**The framework** (`src/17-bosses.js`). A boss is\n473\t`{ kind, x, y, phase, parts: [{ id, ox, oy, r, hp, max, armor, weak, alive }], script, rs }`.\n474\t- Damage goes to the part hit: × `armor` (0.15 means \"TINK\" sparks and no damage number; 1 is normal; 2 is a weak point).\n475\t- A part destroyed: an explosion, debris, ratings +10, and the part's `onDestroy`.\n476\t- Phases are coroutines (`game.script` generators) that yield on time and on conditions. A phase switch cancels the old\n477\t  script and starts the new one.\n478\t- Boss HP bar: top centre, below the ratings gauge, with the boss's name and one segment per part.\n479\t- `bossHp` **(T)** and the player count (×(1 + 0.5 × (players − 1))) scale every HP.\n480\t- **Netplay:** every boss provides `toNet()`, a small array (position, phase, timers, angles, part bits and HP\n481\t  percentages), and `fromNet(a)`, which rebuilds `rs` on clients. All boss drawing reads `rs` only.\n482\t\n483\t**Boss 1: MASHY, \"THE NETWORK'S BELOVED MASCOT, NOW WITH UPGRADES\"** (room 1-B, *SOUNDSTAGE 9: MASHY'S BIG DEBUT*)\n484\t- **Look:** a giant animatronic potato in a tuxedo and bow tie on tank treads, with googly eyes. A **Butter Cannon** on\n485\t  the left arm, a **Gravy Gatling** on the right, and a hatch in its smile.\n486\t- **Size and parts:** about 70 × 50 units.\n487\t  - Body: r 26, HP 160, armor 0.15 while either arm is alive, then 0.5.\n488\t  - Left arm (ox −30, oy 6): r 10, HP 45.\n489\t  - Right arm (ox +30, oy 6): r 10, HP 45.\n490\t  - Mouth hatch (oy 14): r 9, weak ×2, only while open.\n491\t- **Entrance:** the N door bursts open and Mashy rolls in to y 70 (2 s); boss music starts.\n492\t- **Phase 1 (both arms):** it drifts side to side along the north third at speed 30.\n493\t  - Butter Cannon: every 1.8 s, a 5-way spread at the nearest contestant (arc 0.9 rad, speed 95).\n494\t  - Gravy Gatling: every 3.2 s, a 1.2 s stream sweeping 100° (10 bullets/s, speed 120).\n495\t  - When one arm falls (it drops off smoking), the other fires 30 % faster.\n496\t- **Phase 2 (no arms):**\n497\t  - The hatch opens for 2.2 s every 4.5 s.\n498\t  - Head ring: every 2.5 s, 14 orbs at speed 80, offset alternating.\n499\t  - **Tater Tot Toss**: every 5 s, 3 lobbed tots that burst into 6 shards each.\n500\t  - 6 goons from the S door every 9 s.\n501\t- **Phase 3 (body < 35 %): \"MASHY'S GONE MASHY!\"**\n502\t  - Charges: 0.9 s telegraph (revving, exhaust smoke, red eyes, a line on the floor), then 170 u/s toward the target\n503\t    until it hits a wall, where it bounces.\n504\t  - 3 charges, then 2.5 s rest with the hatch open.\n505\t  - 6 clapbots from E/W every 10 s.\n506\t- **Death:** 2 s of chain explosions, beige \"mashed potato\" confetti, a big flash, then a shower of 30 cash pickups, 2\n507\t  prize boxes and 1 capsule. Lance: \"MASHY HAS BEEN... MASHED! SOMEBODY GET A SPATULA!\"\n508\t\n509\t**Boss 2: THE WHEEL OF MISFORTUNE** (room 2-B, *THE BIG SPIN*)\n510\t- **Look:** a giant prize wheel (radius 44) on a mount at the north wall, centre (184, 52).\n511\t  - Eight labelled segments, each with a marquee-bulb cluster: TOMATO TIME, LASER LIGHTS, MIME TIME, BANKRUPT,\n512\t    DISCO FEVER, GOON SQUAD, JACKPOT and SPIN AGAIN.\n513\t  - A clicking pointer on top.\n514\t- **Parts:** 8 bulb clusters (at radius 34, rotating with the wheel, HP 18 each) and the hub **Jackpot Core** (r 14, HP\n515\t  220, armored 0.15 in phase 1).\n516\t- **Phase 1 cycle:**\n517\t  - Spin for 2.5 s. The bulb clusters move, so hitting them is a skill.\n518\t  - It slows and stops on a random living segment, with clicks and a drum roll. Lance announces it: \"LASER LIGHTS!\"\n519\t  - The segment's attack runs for 4–6 s; then the next spin.\n520\t- **Segment attacks:**\n521\t  - TOMATO TIME: 8 tomatoes lobbed from the audience, staggered 0.3 s.\n522\t  - LASER LIGHTS: 4 beams from the hub, each telegraphed with a thin line for 0.8 s, sweeping 1.2 rad over 4 s.\n523\t  - MIME TIME: 6 mimes puff in, scattered around the contestants (never within 40).\n524\t  - BANKRUPT: 2 rings of 20 coin bullets (speed 85, offset), ratings −10, a big \"BANKRUPT!\" sting.\n525\t  - DISCO FEVER: 2 disco balls drop out of the wheel.\n526\t  - GOON SQUAD: 12 goons from E/W/S.\n527\t  - JACKPOT: confetti, 20 cash pickups and 1 capsule rain down; the wheel is stunned for 3 s and the core takes full\n528\t    damage.\n529\t  - SPIN AGAIN: spins again at once, 1.5× faster, and the next attack's bullets are 20 % faster.\n530\t- **Losing segments:** destroying a cluster blacks its segment out (\"VOID\") and removes it from the draw.\n531\t- **Phase 2 (4 segments destroyed): \"THE WHEEL BREAKS LOOSE!\"**\n532\t  - It tears off its mount and rolls around the arena, bouncing off walls at 85 u/s. Contact r 40, dmg 2.\n533\t  - Each bounce sprays 8 sparks (orbs).\n534\t  - It still lands on its remaining segments every 6 s. The core takes full damage.\n535\t- **Death:** it falls flat, spins down like a coin and bursts into bulbs and coins. \"THE WHEEL HAS STOPPED... FOREVER!\"\n536\t\n537\t**Boss 3: LANCE LUSTRE LIVE! → THE NETWORK** (room 3-B, the Season Finale)\n538\t- **Phase A, the STARMAKER 9000.** Lance (a Humanoid at size 1.4) rides a hovering golden podium mech with a spotlight\n539\t  turret on each side.\n540\t  - Parts: podium r 22, HP 260; turrets r 8, HP 30 each.\n541\t  - It hovers and bobs, drifting to stay 100–140 from the contestants. Patterns are scripted in a cycle:\n542\t    1. **CUE CARD CYCLONE:** a 3-arm spiral of spinning card bullets (1.4 rad/s, 12 a second) for 3 s.\n543\t    2. **MIC DROP:** a shadow circle telegraphs the landing (r 30, 1.0 s); it rises, then slams down there. A ring of\n544\t       24 orbs plus a shockwave ring that grows to r 80 (dmg 1). The slide's i-frames get through it, which teaches\n545\t       the slide.\n546\t    3. **SPOTLIGHT SWEEP:** each living turret throws a telegraphed light cone that sweeps the floor. Standing in a lit\n547\t       cone for 0.4 s is a hit. A destroyed turret has no sweep.\n548\t    4. **COMMERCIAL BREAK** (at 66 % and 33 % HP): Lance flies off-screen.\n549\t       - A \"WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK!\" banner and the sponsor jingle.\n550\t       - 12 s of adds: goons, clapbots and 1 brute. The boss is gone and can't be hit.\n551\t       - He returns when the adds are cleared or the timer ends.\n552\t  - **At 0 HP:** the podium crashes. Lance tumbles out and his face *peels off*, showing a speaker grille:\n553\t    \"LANCE WAS A ROBOT ALL ALONG!\"\n554\t- **Phase B, THE NETWORK.** The north wall rises (a tween on the wall art), revealing a wall of **12 TVs** (3 rows × 4)\n555\t  around a giant lens, **THE EYE**.\n556\t  - TVs: parts r 10, HP 22. THE EYE: r 18, HP 300, armored 0.15 until 8 TVs are gone.\n557\t  - Every 4–6 s each TV flips to a channel, with a 0.5 s flicker telegraph. At most 4 TVs are active at once:\n558\t    - STATIC: 5 static sparks aimed at a contestant.\n559\t    - NEWS: after a 0.8 s line telegraph, a beam straight down its column for 1 s.\n560\t    - CARTOON: 2 clapbots pop out.\n561\t    - SHOPPING: drops a cash pickup (bait).\n562\t    - LANCE: Lance's face spits a 3-way spread.\n563\t  - After 8 TVs, THE EYE opens and alternates every 3 s between a spiral (2 arms) and a ring of 18.\n564\t  - **Death:** the screens burst one by one, \"SIGNAL LOST\", and a white static fade. Victory.\n565\t\n566\t### 5.10 Scoring, lives, continue, high scores\n567\t\n568\t- **Score** is **winnings in dollars**, per contestant. There's no separate points counter. Shown as \"$1,234,500\".\n569\t- **Continue:** when every contestant is out, run the CONTINUE countdown from `E.Arcade` (`cab.continue(10, done)`).\n570\t  - \"CONTINUE? 10…0\" with Lance's line.\n571\t  - Any player's confirm or start continues, which needs **engine patch P3**: `continue()` must read every\n572\t    `game.players` input.\n573\t  - On continue, every contestant gets full lives and half their winnings (\"THE NETWORK TAKES ITS CUT!\").\n574\t  - At zero: Game Over.\n575\t- **Game Over:** a sad-trombone sting, \"AND THAT'S A WRAP!\", the prize recap of what they *would* have won (short), then\n576\t  initials.\n577\t- **High scores:** `new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'mashtv', hud: false, idle: 10 })`, one table, mode `'show'`.\n578\t  - After a run, each qualifying contestant enters initials in turn with **their own** input (**engine patch P3:**\n579\t    `cab.enter(score, mode, done, input)`).\n580\t  - Then `cab.drawTable` on the \"TOP EARNERS\" screen.\n581\t  - Episode-select \"rehearsal\" runs and attract demos never enter the table.\n582\t\n583\t### 5.11 Difficulty and player scaling\n584\t\n585\t- Difficulty is chosen before the lobby (ROOKIE / CONTESTANT / CHAMPION; §5.1), stored in `MT.run.diff` and shown in the HUD.\n586\t- Player count scales wave counts (§5.7) and boss HP (§5.9).\n587\t- Every multiplier is visible and live in dev mode.\n588\t\n589\t### 5.12 The broadcast layer (how the show talks)\n590\t\n591\t- **Jumbotron:** a big screen above the north wall in world space. It shows a live `rig.drawPortrait` of whoever is\n592\t  talking (Lance, Penny, or a boss face), with scanlines. Between lines it shows the MASH TV logo, the ratings and a\n593\t  sponsor ad loop.\n594\t- **Lower third:** a bottom-centre banner while someone talks: name plate (LANCE LUSTRE / PENNY PRIZE / ANNOUNCER), the\n595\t  line typing out at 45 chars/s, and the Babble voice (§10.3).\n596\t  - Lines queue with priorities, so a boss intro beats a kill quip.\n597\t  - Quips are rate-limited (at most one per 6 s).\n598\t  - The setting \"Host chatter: Normal / Less / Off\" filters by priority.\n599\t- **Crowd:** the audience sprites bob with R. They cheer at kills, big multi-kills and showboats; \"OOH\" at hits; laugh\n600\t  at deaths; do *the wave* during Prime Time.\n601\t- **Events → reactions** come through one table: `MT.react[event] = { line, crowd, sting, priority }`. Gameplay code only\n602\t  emits events (`world.event('kill', …)`), so it never calls audio or text directly.\n603\t\n604\t---\n605\t\n606\t## 6. Content overview\n607\t\n608\t| Content | Count |\n609\t|---|---|\n610\t| Episodes | 3 (THE PILOT · SWEEPS WEEK · THE SEASON FINALE), each with its own set, music and enemy pool |\n611\t| Rooms | 18 wave rooms (6 per episode) + 3 boss rooms + the Green Room bonus |\n612\t| Session round | THE LIGHTNING ROUND (3 rooms + Mashy, reusing episode rooms) |\n613\t| Enemies | 9 kinds + the Heckler King, prize crates, vault locks |\n614\t| Bosses | 3 (Mashy · the Wheel of Misfortune · Lance in the Starmaker 9000 → The Network) |\n615\t| Power-ups | 5 weapons/add-ons + shield, speed, Showstopper, Encore |\n616\t| Pickups | 4 cash kinds, 18 named prizes, 9 Golden Keys, the Golden Statuette |\n617\t| Hazards | conveyor belts (Ep2), pyro vents (Ep3), tomato splats, land mimes |\n618\t| Characters | 4 contestant looks, Lance Lustre (host), Penny Prize (co-host), the Announcer (voice), the audience, paparazzi |\n619\t| Story beats | Cold Open, 3 episode cards, 3 boss intros and defeats, the robot reveal, 3 Prize Recaps, Ending A, Ending B, Game Over, Continue |\n620\t\n621\t### 6.1 Every episode uses the same map shape\n622\t\n623\t```\n624\t                  [ B: BOSS ]\n625\t                       │\n626\t [ 4: KEY ROOM ] ─► [ 5: ARMORY ] ◄─ [ 6: CASH/BATTLE ]\n627\t       ▲                ▲                  ▲\n628\t [ 2: LEFT ] ◄─── [ 1: START ] ───► [ 3: RIGHT ]\n629\t```\n630\t\n631\t- Exits: 1 → W:2, N:5, E:3. 2 → N:4. 3 → N:6. 4 → E:5. 6 → W:5. 5 → N:B.\n632\t- The paths are **direct** (1→5→B: 2 rooms), **left** (1→2→4→5→B: 4 rooms, 2 keys) and **right** (1→3→6→5→B: 4\n633\t  rooms, 1 key).\n634\t- Walking out of a door enters the next room from the opposite door; that's the room's `entry`. An episode's start\n635\t  room, the Green Room and the Lightning Round's first room are entered from **S**. A boss room is always entered from\n636\t  S, because room 5 leaves by N.\n637\t- **Keys:** 3 per episode, 9 in all. The left path gets 2 per episode. **The Green Room needs 5**, so a team takes the\n638\t  left path at least twice. The \"NEXT ON MASH TV\" card shows key icons on rooms that hold a key.\n639\t\n640\t**Wave notation** in the tables below:\n641\t- `W3 ≤4|@8: N goon×6, E popper×2 · item spread@drop` means: wave 3 starts when 4 or fewer counted enemies are alive,\n642\t  or 8 s after wave 2 started, whichever comes first.\n643\t- It spawns 6 goons from the north door and 2 poppers from the east, and drops a Triple Play capsule from the ceiling.\n644\t- `@2` means 2 s after WAVES begins.\n645\t- Cell positions are interior `[cx, cy]` (0–20, 0–12).\n646\t- `par` is the clear time, in seconds, for the speed bonus.\n647\t\n648\t---\n649\t\n650\t## 7. Episode and room content\n651\t\n652\t### 7.1 EPISODE 1: THE PILOT (Studio 9, set `studio`)\n653\t\n654\tEnemy pool: goon, clapbot, popper, mime. Stunt: 12 clapbots. Music: `studioBattle`.\n655\t\n656\t| id | Name | Type | Cell | Exits | Key | Notes |\n657\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n658\t| 1-1 | OPENING NUMBER | start | (1,2) | W→1-2, N→1-5, E→1-3 | — | tutorial prompts; intros for goon, clapbot and popper |\n659\t| 1-2 | MIME FIELD | battle | (0,2) | N→1-4 | `mimes` | 10 placed mimes; rockets |\n660\t| 1-3 | CLAP TRAP | battle | (2,2) | N→1-6 | — | clapbot-heavy; gold records |\n661\t| 1-4 | KEY GAUNTLET | key (survive) | (0,1) | E→1-5 | `survive` | key in a prize cage that opens at 20 s |\n662\t| 1-5 | WEAPONS LOCKER | armory | (1,1) | N→1-B | — | 3 weapon pedestals; the big room before the boss |\n663\t| 1-6 | CASH COW CORRAL | cash | (2,1) | W→1-5 | `crate` | 6 prize crates; cash ×1.5 |\n664\t| 1-B | MASHY'S BIG DEBUT | boss | (1,0) | — | — | Mashy (§5.9) |\n665\t\n666\t**1-1 OPENING NUMBER** (par 70)\n667\t- W1 @2: N goon×6 (gap 0.35), S goon×6 (gap 0.35).\n668\t- W2 ≤2|@10: E goon×8, W goon×8.\n669\t- W3 ≤4|@8: all goon×3 · item spread@center.\n670\t- W4 ≤4|@8: N clapbot×6, S clapbot×6.\n671\t- W5 ≤5|@8: all goon×5, N popper×2.\n672\t\n673\tTutorial prompts appear once per run, in the input glyphs of each player's last device:\n674\t- At W1: MOVE and AIM+FIRE.\n675\t- At the first capsule: \"WALK OVER POWER-UPS\".\n676\t- At W3: \"SHOWBOAT NEAR ENEMIES FOR RATINGS\".\n677\t- At W4: \"SLIDE THROUGH DANGER\".\n678\t- When 20 or more enemies are alive: \"SHOWSTOPPER CLEARS THE SCREEN\".\n679\t- At EXIT: \"PICK A DOOR!\"\n680\t\n681\t**1-2 MIME FIELD** (par 60). Place mimes at [3,3] [7,2] [13,2] [17,3] [5,6] [15,6] [3,9] [7,10] [13,10] [17,9].\n682\t- W1 @2: S goon×8.\n683\t- W2 ≤3|@8: N popper×2, E goon×8.\n684\t- W3 ≤3|@10: W goon×10 · item rockets@drop.\n685\t- W4 ≤4|@8: all clapbot×3.\n686\t- W5 ≤3|@8: N popper×3, S popper×3, E goon×6.\n687\t- Key `mimes`: when all 10 placed mimes are destroyed, the key drops where the last one stood. Lance: \"MIME OVER MATTER!\"\n688\t\n689\t**1-3 CLAP TRAP** (par 65)\n690\t- W1 @2: E clapbot×8, W clapbot×8.\n691\t- W2 ≤3|@8: N goon×12.\n692\t- W3 ≤4|@8: all clapbot×5 · item records@drop.\n693\t- W4 ≤4|@8: S popper×4, E goon×8.\n694\t- W5 ≤3|@8: all clapbot×6, N goon×6.\n695\t\n696\t**1-4 KEY GAUNTLET** (survive 35 s)\n697\t- The key sits on a turning pedestal at the centre inside a **prize cage**: a solid ring of r 14 that blocks contestants.\n698\t  The cage lifts at 20 s with a fanfare.\n699\t- For 35 s, streams arrive:\n700\t  - Every 1.2 s, 1 goon from each door."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eec69157-3f75-40b4-be93-e6ea9b3a321a","uuid":"389dfd89-ba37-412d-b334-10d5bf3d71fe","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:16.514Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050305__x4339a3/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **Drops** on enemy death roll the enemy's drop table (§5.8) × `dropMul` **(T)**. Floor caps: at most 3 capsules and\n  25 cash pickups at once.\n- **Prize crates** are placed props: HP 3, solid while whole (`map.solid`, or a static body). When broken they spill\n  3–5 cash, a 50 % chance of a prize, and the key if the room's data says so.\n\n### 5.4 Ratings (the show's heartbeat)\n\n- `R` runs 0–100 and is **shared by the team**: it's the show's rating, not a player's. It's drawn top-centre as a big TV\n  \"RATINGS\" gauge with a needle, the multiplier and an APPLAUSE light.\n- **Gains:**\n  - A kill adds the enemy's `rat` value. A multi-kill adds +2 for each kill past 2 within 0.4 s.\n  - Showboat (§5.1).\n  - A **near miss**: +0.5 when a foe bullet passes within 7 units of a contestant without hitting (at most 3 a second).\n  - A prize +2, a key +5, a boss part destroyed +10.\n  - All gains × `ratingsGain` **(T)**.\n- **Losses:** a hit −12; a death −25; BANKRUPT (the wheel) −10.\n- **Decay:** after 2.5 s without a gain, R falls by `ratingsDecay` **(T)** 2.5 a second.\n- **Multiplier:** R < 20 ×1; < 40 ×2; < 60 ×3; < 80 ×4; ≥ 80 ×5.\n- **PRIME TIME** when R reaches 100. It lasts `primeTime` **(T)** 12 s:\n  - The multiplier is locked at ×5.\n  - A \"PRIME TIME!\" banner and fanfare sting; `audio.layer('prime', 1, .3)` brings the brass in.\n  - The audience throws 3 random capsules in arcs from the bleachers; confetti cannons fire; the APPLAUSE sign blinks.\n  - Afterwards R = 60, with a 20 s cooldown before the next Prime Time.\n- **RATINGS STUNT** (anti-stall): if R < 5 for 10 s during waves, \"WE'RE LOSING VIEWERS!\" and the producers release the\n  episode's stunt from a random door:\n  - Ep1: 12 clapbots.\n  - Ep2: a dolly tank.\n  - Ep3: a mascot brute.\n\n  R +15. At most once per room.\n\n### 5.5 Arena, doors and hazards\n\n**Geometry, the same in every room.** A TileMap of 23 × 15 cells is 368 × 240 world units.\n- **Walls:** row 0, row 14, col 0 and col 22, wall type 1: `h: 26`, studio-flat faces (§9.2).\n  - The south wall row is `cut: true`, so it never hides the floor from the camera.\n- **Interior:** 21 × 13 cells, x 16–352, y 16–224, centre **(184, 120)**.\n- **Door gaps** (3 cells, wall type 2, painted by our door painter):\n  - N: cols 10–12 of row 0. S: cols 10–12 of row 14. W: rows 6–8 of col 0. E: rows 6–8 of col 22.\n  - Door centres: N (184, 8), S (184, 232), W (8, 120), E (360, 120).\n- **Room data uses interior cells** `[cx, cy]`, cx 0–20 and cy 0–12. In world units that's\n  `(24 + cx * 16, 24 + cy * 16)`.\n\n**Door states:**\n- `closed`.\n- `opening`: 0.35 s; the shutter rolls up, a red beacon and a klaxon.\n- `open`: spawning.\n- `closing`: 0.3 s; a slam and dust.\n- `exit`: a green beacon and a lit sign above the door with the destination's name and room-type icon. Its cells become\n  walkable (`map.set(cx, cy, 0)`), with an exit trigger 10 units past the threshold.\n\n**Spawning:**\n- From a **door:** enemies appear 20 units outside the gap and walk in with wall collision off (\"entering\") until inside\n  the interior. The door stays open while its queue has spawns, plus 0.6 s.\n- From the **audience** (hecklers): a leap from the E or W bleachers over the wall. An arc from x −30 or 398 to a random\n  interior point on that side; 0.7 s, invulnerable in the air.\n- **Drop:** from the ceiling at a random free interior point at least 50 units from every contestant. A shadow\n  telegraphs for 0.6 s, then it falls.\n\n**Hazards:**\n- **Conveyor belts** (Ep2): strips 2 cells tall across the room. Each pushes everything on it (contestants, enemies,\n  pickups, the key) at ±40 u/s, with animated chevrons. Direction reverses every 12 s after a 1.5 s warning (lights, an\n  alarm, the belt slowing).\n- **Pyro vents** (Ep3): floor grates firing in data-driven patterns.\n  - Telegraph: 1.0 s of glow, sparks and rumble.\n  - Then a 1.2 s flame column, r 12: 1 damage to contestants, 3 damage a second to enemies. It's emissive and casts light.\n- **Tomato splats:** puddles of r 14 for 6 s that slow contestants to ×0.6.\n- **Prize crates** and **vault locks:** static targets (rooms 1-6, 2-6, 3-4).\n\n**Camera:**\n- Fixed: `game.focus(184, 120, 0)` every update.\n- Zoom is fitted so the walled arena fills the screen, leaving ~22 px top and bottom for the HUD. Measure\n  `map.bounds(game.view)` at zoom 1 and recompute when the screen changes size (`game.screen.listeners`). Clamp to\n  [0.6, 1.6], then × `camZoom` **(T)**.\n- The scene's `camera: { zoom: false }` turns the player's zoom off. Shake goes through `game.shake` (comfort settings\n  apply).\n- Wide or tall screens show the studio around the arena (bleachers, cranes, the jumbotron; §9.2).\n\n### 5.6 Room flow (phases)\n\n`ENTER` → `INTRO` → `WAVES` → `CLEAR` → `EXIT` → `TRANSITION` → the next room's `ENTER`.\n\n- **ENTER** (1.2 s): the walk-in. The door behind the contestants slams.\n- **INTRO** (≤ 2 s): Lance's room line on the jumbotron and a \"MASH!\" stinger. An episode's first room is preceded by the\n  episode card (§11.3).\n- **WAVES:** the room script (§5.7) runs.\n- **CLEAR:** every wave has spawned and no counted enemy is alive. Mimes, crates and vault locks don't count.\n  - \"ROOM CLEAR!\" banner and sting.\n  - Each living contestant gets a clear bonus of `$1,000 × episode × multiplier`, +50 % if cleared under the room's\n    `par` seconds.\n  - A Lance line. Remaining foe bullets fade out.\n- **EXIT:** the exit doors open with their signs. The first contestant into an exit trigger picks it; 0.8 s later every\n  contestant goes. Pickups can still be collected meanwhile.\n  - If nobody leaves within 25 s: \"HURRY UP!\" and 4 clapbots every 6 s from the doors that aren't exits.\n- **TRANSITION:** a 0.4 s TV-static wipe, then the \"NEXT ON MASH TV\" map card (2.5 s, skippable with confirm), then\n  another static wipe into the next room.\n\n**Boss rooms:** `ENTER` → `BOSS_INTRO` (~4 s cutscene, skippable) → `BOSS` → `BOSS_DEATH` (3 s) → `CLEAR` → the `recap`\nscene.\n\n**Survive rooms** (1-4): `WAVES` ends when the timer runs out and the field is clear.\n\n### 5.7 Waves: the room script data format\n\n```js\n// src/20-content-*.js — one room\n{ id: '1-2', name: 'MIME FIELD', ep: 1, type: 'battle', cell: [0, 2], exits: { N: '1-4' }, par: 60,\n  place: [['mime', 4, 3], ['mime', 10, 2] /* … */],      // [kind, cx, cy] at room start (interior cells)\n  items: [[1.5, 'spread', [5, 6]]],                      // [seconds after WAVES starts, pickup, 'center' | 'drop' | [cx, cy]]\n  key: { rule: 'mimes' },                                 // 'mimes' | 'place' | 'crate' | 'carrier' | 'vault' | 'final' | 'survive'\n  hazards: [],                                            // e.g. { kind: 'conveyor', rows: [3, 6, 9], dirs: [1, -1, 1] }\n  waves: [\n    { at: 2, spawn: [['S', 'goon', 8]] },\n    { left: 3, at: 8, spawn: [['N', 'popper', 2], ['E', 'goon', 8]] },\n    { left: 3, at: 10, spawn: [['W', 'goon', 10]], items: [['rockets', 'drop']] },\n  ] }\n```\n\n- **When a wave starts:** `at` seconds after the previous wave started, or when no more than `left` counted enemies are\n  alive, whichever comes first. With only one of them given, that one alone. Build it as one `game.script` per room:\n  `yield E.any([w.at, () => alive() <= w.left])`.\n- **A spawn entry** is `[door, kind, n, gap = 0.25]`. Doors:\n  - `N`, `E`, `S`, `W` for one door.\n  - `all` (each door gets n), `sides` (E and W), `ends` (N and S).\n  - `audience`, `drop`, or `[cx, cy]` for an exact cell.\n- **Scaling:** `n' = round(n × (1 + 0.35 × (players − 1)) × waveSize (T) × difficulty)`, where difficulty is ROOKIE 0.8,\n  CONTESTANT 1 or CHAMPION 1.2. Lower `spawnGap` **(T)** packs the spawns tighter.\n- **The room ends** when the last wave has spawned and the field is clear. With `{ final: true, script: 'name' }` a wave\n  runs a named scripted event (the Pyro Pit's FINALE BURST).\n\n### 5.8 Enemies\n\nAll enemies share an archetype record:\n`{ kind, hp, speed, r, contact, cash, rat, drops, make(world, x, y, o), update(e, dt, world), draw(r, e) }`.\n\nEach draws from `e.rs`, a render state `{ x, y, z, face, vx, vy, state, t, hpPct, flash, alpha }`, so the same draw code\nworks on hub clients (§14.3). Common rules:\n- Target the nearest living contestant. Separate from each other with an `E.SpatialHash` (radius 10, a soft push), so\n  crowds don't stack.\n- Telegraph every attack with a visible wind-up of at least 0.3 s.\n- On a hit, flash white (`r.actor(..., { flash })`) with a small knockback.\n- On death, a confetti burst in the enemy's palette (`particles.bits`), a cash pop-up, a pop sound and the drop roll.\n- `enemySpeed`, `enemyHp`, `enemyBulletSpeed` and `contactDmg` are **(T)** multipliers.\n\n| kind | HP | Speed | Behaviour | Telegraph | Cash / rat | Drops |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `goon` (STUDIO SECURITY) | 1 | 52 ±6 | Walks straight at the target in loose flocks. Within 16 units, a baton swing (`E.Attack('bash')`, wind 0.3 s, reach 14). Contact dmg 1. | the baton rises (wind) | $100 / 1 | bill 8 %, capsule 1.2 %, prize 1 % |\n| `clapbot` (APPLAUSE ROBOT) | 1 | hop 115 | Hops every 0.4 s toward the target ±40° (erratic). Clapper hands clap on each hop. Contact dmg 1. | squash before the hop | $150 / 1 | bill 10 % |\n| `popper` (PARTY POPPER) | 2 | 38 | Waddles to the target. Within 18 units it lights its fuse (0.6 s: inflates, flashes, hisses), then bursts into a ring of 8 confetti shards (speed 90, life 1.2 s). It also bursts when killed. | swelling and a fuse spark | $250 / 2 | stack 10 %, capsule 3 % |\n| `mime` (LAND MIME) | 1 | 0 | Stands still, half-visible (alpha 0.45), miming \"trapped in a box\". When a contestant is within 34 units: a 0.7 s telegraph (hands up, shaking, beeps), then a blast of r 36 (dmg 1). Shot first, it pops harmlessly. **Doesn't count for room clear.** | a beep and shaking | $300 / 2 | bill 30 % |\n| `disco` (DISCO BALL) | 5 (big: 10) | 70 | Bounces diagonally off walls. Every 3 s, 4 light shots in a + or × pattern, alternating (speed 110). A **big** one splits into 2 small ones (HP 3) when it dies. Contact dmg 1. | facets flare 0.4 s | $400 (big $800) / 3 | stack 20 %, capsule 5 % |\n| `heckler` (STUDIO AUDIENCE) | 3 | 45 | Arrives over the wall. Keeps 70–110 units from the target and strafes. Every 2.2 s lobs a rotten tomato (`E.arc` to where the target will be in 0.6 s); the splat does dmg 1 within r 10 and leaves a slow puddle. | a red ring on the floor where it lands, the throw pose (`E.MOVES.throw`) | $350 / 2 | prize 6 %, capsule 4 % |\n| `tank` (DOLLY TANK) | 14 | 26 | A camera dolly turned tank. The chassis turns slowly; the camera-turret tracks the target at 1.4 rad/s. Every 2.4 s it fires a shell (speed 120) that explodes at walls or contestants (r 16, dmg 1). On death it explodes, damaging enemies too. | lens flash and an aim line, 0.4 s | $1,000 / 6 | case 15 %, capsule 15 % |\n| `snake` (CABLE SNAKE) | head 8, segments 2 × 10 | 60 | A head plug and 10 cable segments that follow the head's path history (one point every 6 units). It weaves toward the target. Shot-off segments shorten it; segments can be hit independently. Contact dmg 1. | the head rears back before a 1.5× lunge | head $1,200 / 5, seg $150 / 1 | head: case 30 % |\n| `brute` (THE CEREAL KILLER, a mascot) | 24 | walk 40, charge 220 | Walks at the target. Every 4 s: a 0.8 s telegraph (stomps, floor rings, a roar), then a straight charge of up to 1.4 s. Hitting a wall stuns it for 1.5 s, and stunned it takes ×2 damage. Contact dmg 2. | a stomp, rings on the floor, a red line along the charge | $2,000 / 8 | case 40 %, capsule 25 % |\n| `hecklerKing` (2-4 only) | 12 | 45 | A heckler with a foam crown who throws 3-tomato volleys. Carries the room's key. | as heckler | $1,500 / 6 | key |\n| `crate` | 3 | — | A static prize crate (see §5.3). | — | — | cash, prize, key |\n| `lock` (3-4 only) | 15 | — | A vault bolt on the north wall; when all 4 break, the safe opens. | — | $500 / 2 | — |\n\nEnemy foe-bullet kinds, used across enemies and bosses:\n- `orb` (generic): r 3.\n- `shard` (confetti): r 2.\n- `beam` (disco light): r 2, long.\n- `tomato`: a lob with z.\n- `shell`: explodes.\n- `butter`, `gravy`, `coin`, `card` (spins), `static` (jittery), `tot` (lobbed, bursts into 6 shards).\n\nSpeeds stay at 70–130, readable at 10 feet, each with a bright core and a dark outline.\n\n### 5.9 Bosses\n\n**The framework** (`src/17-bosses.js`). A boss is\n`{ kind, x, y, phase, parts: [{ id, ox, oy, r, hp, max, armor, weak, alive }], script, rs }`.\n- Damage goes to the part hit: × `armor` (0.15 means \"TINK\" sparks and no damage number; 1 is normal; 2 is a weak point).\n- A part destroyed: an explosion, debris, ratings +10, and the part's `onDestroy`.\n- Phases are coroutines (`game.script` generators) that yield on time and on conditions. A phase switch cancels the old\n  script and starts the new one.\n- Boss HP bar: top centre, below the ratings gauge, with the boss's name and one segment per part.\n- `bossHp` **(T)** and the player count (×(1 + 0.5 × (players − 1))) scale every HP.\n- **Netplay:** every boss provides `toNet()`, a small array (position, phase, timers, angles, part bits and HP\n  percentages), and `fromNet(a)`, which rebuilds `rs` on clients. All boss drawing reads `rs` only.\n\n**Boss 1: MASHY, \"THE NETWORK'S BELOVED MASCOT, NOW WITH UPGRADES\"** (room 1-B, *SOUNDSTAGE 9: MASHY'S BIG DEBUT*)\n- **Look:** a giant animatronic potato in a tuxedo and bow tie on tank treads, with googly eyes. A **Butter Cannon** on\n  the left arm, a **Gravy Gatling** on the right, and a hatch in its smile.\n- **Size and parts:** about 70 × 50 units.\n  - Body: r 26, HP 160, armor 0.15 while either arm is alive, then 0.5.\n  - Left arm (ox −30, oy 6): r 10, HP 45.\n  - Right arm (ox +30, oy 6): r 10, HP 45.\n  - Mouth hatch (oy 14): r 9, weak ×2, only while open.\n- **Entrance:** the N door bursts open and Mashy rolls in to y 70 (2 s); boss music starts.\n- **Phase 1 (both arms):** it drifts side to side along the north third at speed 30.\n  - Butter Cannon: every 1.8 s, a 5-way spread at the nearest contestant (arc 0.9 rad, speed 95).\n  - Gravy Gatling: every 3.2 s, a 1.2 s stream sweeping 100° (10 bullets/s, speed 120).\n  - When one arm falls (it drops off smoking), the other fires 30 % faster.\n- **Phase 2 (no arms):**\n  - The hatch opens for 2.2 s every 4.5 s.\n  - Head ring: every 2.5 s, 14 orbs at speed 80, offset alternating.\n  - **Tater Tot Toss**: every 5 s, 3 lobbed tots that burst into 6 shards each.\n  - 6 goons from the S door every 9 s.\n- **Phase 3 (body < 35 %): \"MASHY'S GONE MASHY!\"**\n  - Charges: 0.9 s telegraph (revving, exhaust smoke, red eyes, a line on the floor), then 170 u/s toward the target\n    until it hits a wall, where it bounces.\n  - 3 charges, then 2.5 s rest with the hatch open.\n  - 6 clapbots from E/W every 10 s.\n- **Death:** 2 s of chain explosions, beige \"mashed potato\" confetti, a big flash, then a shower of 30 cash pickups, 2\n  prize boxes and 1 capsule. Lance: \"MASHY HAS BEEN... MASHED! SOMEBODY GET A SPATULA!\"\n\n**Boss 2: THE WHEEL OF MISFORTUNE** (room 2-B, *THE BIG SPIN*)\n- **Look:** a giant prize wheel (radius 44) on a mount at the north wall, centre (184, 52).\n  - Eight labelled segments, each with a marquee-bulb cluster: TOMATO TIME, LASER LIGHTS, MIME TIME, BANKRUPT,\n    DISCO FEVER, GOON SQUAD, JACKPOT and SPIN AGAIN.\n  - A clicking pointer on top.\n- **Parts:** 8 bulb clusters (at radius 34, rotating with the wheel, HP 18 each) and the hub **Jackpot Core** (r 14, HP\n  220, armored 0.15 in phase 1).\n- **Phase 1 cycle:**\n  - Spin for 2.5 s. The bulb clusters move, so hitting them is a skill.\n  - It slows and stops on a random living segment, with clicks and a drum roll. Lance announces it: \"LASER LIGHTS!\"\n  - The segment's attack runs for 4–6 s; then the next spin.\n- **Segment attacks:**\n  - TOMATO TIME: 8 tomatoes lobbed from the audience, staggered 0.3 s.\n  - LASER LIGHTS: 4 beams from the hub, each telegraphed with a thin line for 0.8 s, sweeping 1.2 rad over 4 s.\n  - MIME TIME: 6 mimes puff in, scattered around the contestants (never within 40).\n  - BANKRUPT: 2 rings of 20 coin bullets (speed 85, offset), ratings −10, a big \"BANKRUPT!\" sting.\n  - DISCO FEVER: 2 disco balls drop out of the wheel.\n  - GOON SQUAD: 12 goons from E/W/S.\n  - JACKPOT: confetti, 20 cash pickups and 1 capsule rain down; the wheel is stunned for 3 s and the core takes full\n    damage.\n  - SPIN AGAIN: spins again at once, 1.5× faster, and the next attack's bullets are 20 % faster.\n- **Losing segments:** destroying a cluster blacks its segment out (\"VOID\") and removes it from the draw.\n- **Phase 2 (4 segments destroyed): \"THE WHEEL BREAKS LOOSE!\"**\n  - It tears off its mount and rolls around the arena, bouncing off walls at 85 u/s. Contact r 40, dmg 2.\n  - Each bounce sprays 8 sparks (orbs).\n  - It still lands on its remaining segments every 6 s. The core takes full damage.\n- **Death:** it falls flat, spins down like a coin and bursts into bulbs and coins. \"THE WHEEL HAS STOPPED... FOREVER!\"\n\n**Boss 3: LANCE LUSTRE LIVE! → THE NETWORK** (room 3-B, the Season Finale)\n- **Phase A, the STARMAKER 9000.** Lance (a Humanoid at size 1.4) rides a hovering golden podium mech with a spotlight\n  turret on each side.\n  - Parts: podium r 22, HP 260; turrets r 8, HP 30 each.\n  - It hovers and bobs, drifting to stay 100–140 from the contestants. Patterns are scripted in a cycle:\n    1. **CUE CARD CYCLONE:** a 3-arm spiral of spinning card bullets (1.4 rad/s, 12 a second) for 3 s.\n    2. **MIC DROP:** a shadow circle telegraphs the landing (r 30, 1.0 s); it rises, then slams down there. A ring of\n       24 orbs plus a shockwave ring that grows to r 80 (dmg 1). The slide's i-frames get through it, which teaches\n       the slide.\n    3. **SPOTLIGHT SWEEP:** each living turret throws a telegraphed light cone that sweeps the floor. Standing in a lit\n       cone for 0.4 s is a hit. A destroyed turret has no sweep.\n    4. **COMMERCIAL BREAK** (at 66 % and 33 % HP): Lance flies off-screen.\n       - A \"WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK!\" banner and the sponsor jingle.\n       - 12 s of adds: goons, clapbots and 1 brute. The boss is gone and can't be hit.\n       - He returns when the adds are cleared or the timer ends.\n  - **At 0 HP:** the podium crashes. Lance tumbles out and his face *peels off*, showing a speaker grille:\n    \"LANCE WAS A ROBOT ALL ALONG!\"\n- **Phase B, THE NETWORK.** The north wall rises (a tween on the wall art), revealing a wall of **12 TVs** (3 rows × 4)\n  around a giant lens, **THE EYE**.\n  - TVs: parts r 10, HP 22. THE EYE: r 18, HP 300, armored 0.15 until 8 TVs are gone.\n  - Every 4–6 s each TV flips to a channel, with a 0.5 s flicker telegraph. At most 4 TVs are active at once:\n    - STATIC: 5 static sparks aimed at a contestant.\n    - NEWS: after a 0.8 s line telegraph, a beam straight down its column for 1 s.\n    - CARTOON: 2 clapbots pop out.\n    - SHOPPING: drops a cash pickup (bait).\n    - LANCE: Lance's face spits a 3-way spread.\n  - After 8 TVs, THE EYE opens and alternates every 3 s between a spiral (2 arms) and a ring of 18.\n  - **Death:** the screens burst one by one, \"SIGNAL LOST\", and a white static fade. Victory.\n\n### 5.10 Scoring, lives, continue, high scores\n\n- **Score** is **winnings in dollars**, per contestant. There's no separate points counter. Shown as \"$1,234,500\".\n- **Continue:** when every contestant is out, run the CONTINUE countdown from `E.Arcade` (`cab.continue(10, done)`).\n  - \"CONTINUE? 10…0\" with Lance's line.\n  - Any player's confirm or start continues, which needs **engine patch P3**: `continue()` must read every\n    `game.players` input.\n  - On continue, every contestant gets full lives and half their winnings (\"THE NETWORK TAKES ITS CUT!\").\n  - At zero: Game Over.\n- **Game Over:** a sad-trombone sting, \"AND THAT'S A WRAP!\", the prize recap of what they *would* have won (short), then\n  initials.\n- **High scores:** `new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'mashtv', hud: false, idle: 10 })`, one table, mode `'show'`.\n  - After a run, each qualifying contestant enters initials in turn with **their own** input (**engine patch P3:**\n    `cab.enter(score, mode, done, input)`).\n  - Then `cab.drawTable` on the \"TOP EARNERS\" screen.\n  - Episode-select \"rehearsal\" runs and attract demos never enter the table.\n\n### 5.11 Difficulty and player scaling\n\n- Difficulty is chosen before the lobby (ROOKIE / CONTESTANT / CHAMPION; §5.1), stored in `MT.run.diff` and shown in the HUD.\n- Player count scales wave counts (§5.7) and boss HP (§5.9).\n- Every multiplier is visible and live in dev mode.\n\n### 5.12 The broadcast layer (how the show talks)\n\n- **Jumbotron:** a big screen above the north wall in world space. It shows a live `rig.drawPortrait` of whoever is\n  talking (Lance, Penny, or a boss face), with scanlines. Between lines it shows the MASH TV logo, the ratings and a\n  sponsor ad loop.\n- **Lower third:** a bottom-centre banner while someone talks: name plate (LANCE LUSTRE / PENNY PRIZE / ANNOUNCER), the\n  line typing out at 45 chars/s, and the Babble voice (§10.3).\n  - Lines queue with priorities, so a boss intro beats a kill quip.\n  - Quips are rate-limited (at most one per 6 s).\n  - The setting \"Host chatter: Normal / Less / Off\" filters by priority.\n- **Crowd:** the audience sprites bob with R. They cheer at kills, big multi-kills and showboats; \"OOH\" at hits; laugh\n  at deaths; do *the wave* during Prime Time.\n- **Events → reactions** come through one table: `MT.react[event] = { line, crowd, sting, priority }`. Gameplay code only\n  emits events (`world.event('kill', …)`), so it never calls audio or text directly.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Content overview\n\n| Content | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Episodes | 3 (THE PILOT · SWEEPS WEEK · THE SEASON FINALE), each with its own set, music and enemy pool |\n| Rooms | 18 wave rooms (6 per episode) + 3 boss rooms + the Green Room bonus |\n| Session round | THE LIGHTNING ROUND (3 rooms + Mashy, reusing episode rooms) |\n| Enemies | 9 kinds + the Heckler King, prize crates, vault locks |\n| Bosses | 3 (Mashy · the Wheel of Misfortune · Lance in the Starmaker 9000 → The Network) |\n| Power-ups | 5 weapons/add-ons + shield, speed, Showstopper, Encore |\n| Pickups | 4 cash kinds, 18 named prizes, 9 Golden Keys, the Golden Statuette |\n| Hazards | conveyor belts (Ep2), pyro vents (Ep3), tomato splats, land mimes |\n| Characters | 4 contestant looks, Lance Lustre (host), Penny Prize (co-host), the Announcer (voice), the audience, paparazzi |\n| Story beats | Cold Open, 3 episode cards, 3 boss intros and defeats, the robot reveal, 3 Prize Recaps, Ending A, Ending B, Game Over, Continue |\n\n### 6.1 Every episode uses the same map shape\n\n```\n                  [ B: BOSS ]\n                       │\n [ 4: KEY ROOM ] ─► [ 5: ARMORY ] ◄─ [ 6: CASH/BATTLE ]\n       ▲                ▲                  ▲\n [ 2: LEFT ] ◄─── [ 1: START ] ───► [ 3: RIGHT ]\n```\n\n- Exits: 1 → W:2, N:5, E:3. 2 → N:4. 3 → N:6. 4 → E:5. 6 → W:5. 5 → N:B.\n- The paths are **direct** (1→5→B: 2 rooms), **left** (1→2→4→5→B: 4 rooms, 2 keys) and **right** (1→3→6→5→B: 4\n  rooms, 1 key).\n- Walking out of a door enters the next room from the opposite door; that's the room's `entry`. An episode's start\n  room, the Green Room and the Lightning Round's first room are entered from **S**. A boss room is always entered from\n  S, because room 5 leaves by N.\n- **Keys:** 3 per episode, 9 in all. The left path gets 2 per episode. **The Green Room needs 5**, so a team takes the\n  left path at least twice. The \"NEXT ON MASH TV\" card shows key icons on rooms that hold a key.\n\n**Wave notation** in the tables below:\n- `W3 ≤4|@8: N goon×6, E popper×2 · item spread@drop` means: wave 3 starts when 4 or fewer counted enemies are alive,\n  or 8 s after wave 2 started, whichever comes first.\n- It spawns 6 goons from the north door and 2 poppers from the east, and drops a Triple Play capsule from the ceiling.\n- `@2` means 2 s after WAVES begins.\n- Cell positions are interior `[cx, cy]` (0–20, 0–12).\n- `par` is the clear time, in seconds, for the speed bonus.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Episode and room content\n\n### 7.1 EPISODE 1: THE PILOT (Studio 9, set `studio`)\n\nEnemy pool: goon, clapbot, popper, mime. Stunt: 12 clapbots. Music: `studioBattle`.\n\n| id | Name | Type | Cell | Exits | Key | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1-1 | OPENING NUMBER | start | (1,2) | W→1-2, N→1-5, E→1-3 | — | tutorial prompts; intros for goon, clapbot and popper |\n| 1-2 | MIME FIELD | battle | (0,2) | N→1-4 | `mimes` | 10 placed mimes; rockets |\n| 1-3 | CLAP TRAP | battle | (2,2) | N→1-6 | — | clapbot-heavy; gold records |\n| 1-4 | KEY GAUNTLET | key (survive) | (0,1) | E→1-5 | `survive` | key in a prize cage that opens at 20 s |\n| 1-5 | WEAPONS LOCKER | armory | (1,1) | N→1-B | — | 3 weapon pedestals; the big room before the boss |\n| 1-6 | CASH COW CORRAL | cash | (2,1) | W→1-5 | `crate` | 6 prize crates; cash ×1.5 |\n| 1-B | MASHY'S BIG DEBUT | boss | (1,0) | — | — | Mashy (§5.9) |\n\n**1-1 OPENING NUMBER** (par 70)\n- W1 @2: N goon×6 (gap 0.35), S goon×6 (gap 0.35).\n- W2 ≤2|@10: E goon×8, W goon×8.\n- W3 ≤4|@8: all goon×3 · item spread@center.\n- W4 ≤4|@8: N clapbot×6, S clapbot×6.\n- W5 ≤5|@8: all goon×5, N popper×2.\n\nTutorial prompts appear once per run, in the input glyphs of each player's last device:\n- At W1: MOVE and AIM+FIRE.\n- At the first capsule: \"WALK OVER POWER-UPS\".\n- At W3: \"SHOWBOAT NEAR ENEMIES FOR RATINGS\".\n- At W4: \"SLIDE THROUGH DANGER\".\n- When 20 or more enemies are alive: \"SHOWSTOPPER CLEARS THE SCREEN\".\n- At EXIT: \"PICK A DOOR!\"\n\n**1-2 MIME FIELD** (par 60). Place mimes at [3,3] [7,2] [13,2] [17,3] [5,6] [15,6] [3,9] [7,10] [13,10] [17,9].\n- W1 @2: S goon×8.\n- W2 ≤3|@8: N popper×2, E goon×8.\n- W3 ≤3|@10: W goon×10 · item rockets@drop.\n- W4 ≤4|@8: all clapbot×3.\n- W5 ≤3|@8: N popper×3, S popper×3, E goon×6.\n- Key `mimes`: when all 10 placed mimes are destroyed, the key drops where the last one stood. Lance: \"MIME OVER MATTER!\"\n\n**1-3 CLAP TRAP** (par 65)\n- W1 @2: E clapbot×8, W clapbot×8.\n- W2 ≤3|@8: N goon×12.\n- W3 ≤4|@8: all clapbot×5 · item records@drop.\n- W4 ≤4|@8: S popper×4, E goon×8.\n- W5 ≤3|@8: all clapbot×6, N goon×6.\n\n**1-4 KEY GAUNTLET** (survive 35 s)\n- The key sits on a turning pedestal at the centre inside a **prize cage**: a solid ring of r 14 that blocks contestants.\n  The cage lifts at 20 s with a fanfare.\n- For 35 s, streams arrive:\n  - Every 1.2 s, 1 goon from each door.","numLines":400,"startLine":301,"totalLines":2017}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QCgRDJC8HDS3DK9aJDzwhK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
