{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrZz3L3qr5mkYHCASRo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EFcWZsbvowXmp98VSBZ24A","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n '^#' AI_GUIDE.md | head -120; echo ----; grep -n -i 'twin' AI_GUIDE.md | head; echo ----; grep -n -i 'Arcade' API-INDEX.md | head -60","description":"Find twin-stick and arcade references in engine docs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36418,"cache_read_input_tokens":101635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36418},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eec69157-3f75-40b4-be93-e6ea9b3a321a","uuid":"8289a4c4-99c1-4520-8d0f-66e2ab65a32f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:50.643Z","request_id":"req_011CghrZyoSkTwwLi4aEqAJR","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EFcWZsbvowXmp98VSBZ24A":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050305__x4339a3/work/MashTV-SmashTV-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050305/.cache/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n '^#' AI_GUIDE.md | head -120; echo ----; grep -n -i 'twin' AI_GUIDE.md | head; echo ----; grep -n -i 'Arcade' API-INDEX.md | head -60","description":"Find twin-stick and arcade references in engine docs"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01EFcWZsbvowXmp98VSBZ24A":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050305__x4339a3/work/MashTV-SmashTV-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050305/.cache/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFcWZsbvowXmp98VSBZ24A","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# my-3D2dge guide for AI models\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back\n----\n575:**Twin-stick shooter (Robotron 2084, Smash TV).** Start from the ADVENTURE kit (a `Body` hero in rooms) with the SHOOTER's ships and bullets.\n----\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n1220:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1223:- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1225:- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n1226:- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n1227:- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n1228:- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n1229:- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n1230:- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n1231:- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n1232:- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n1233:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n1234:- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n1235:- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n1236:- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n1237:- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n1238:- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n1239:- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n1240:- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1242:- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n1243:- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n1244:- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n1245:- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n1246:- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n1247:- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n1248:- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n1249:- `arcade.o`: the options\n1250:- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n1251:- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\n1252:- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\n1253:- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eec69157-3f75-40b4-be93-e6ea9b3a321a","uuid":"7c47d909-0bf9-4445-9f2a-277fdd15e666","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:50.666Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# my-3D2dge guide for AI models\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back\n----\n575:**Twin-stick shooter (Robotron 2084, Smash TV).** Start from the ADVENTURE kit (a `Body` hero in rooms) with the SHOOTER's ships and bullets.\n----\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n1220:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1223:- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1225:- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n1226:- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n1227:- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n1228:- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n1229:- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n1230:- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n1231:- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n1232:- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n1233:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n1234:- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n1235:- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n1236:- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n1237:- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n1238:- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n1239:- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n1240:- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1242:- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n1243:- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n1244:- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n1245:- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n1246:- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n1247:- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n1248:- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n1249:- `arcade.o`: the options\n1250:- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n1251:- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\n1252:- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\n1253:- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EFcWZsbvowXmp98VSBZ24A","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
