{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghuAD8ZPqwbdx2yELoTT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is built and playable in its core form. The goal is not met, though. The TASK requires AI Hub online play, and I did not build it, so the stop condition still isn't satisfied.\n\n**Deliverables** (in the work folder root, beside TASK.md)\n- `MashTV-SmashTV-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050305.html`: a single self-contained file with the patched engine and game inlined. It loads from `file://` with no outside requests.\n- `exit-interview.json`: parses, and has the TASK shape with every field filled.\n- The dev folder `MashTV-SmashTV-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050305/` holds the source in `src/`, the engine copy and `engine/PATCHES.md`, the build and test tools, and screenshots in `shots/`.\n\n**Verified**\n- `npm test`-style runner: 119 checks passed, 0 failed.\n- A bot-driven full run goes through all three episodes, the Mashy, Wheel and Lance/Network bosses, the recap handoffs, the endings and the scores screen. It also reaches the Green Room, and a champion run reaches game over.\n- Real Chromium with real key presses: the menus navigate, WASD moves, the arrows fire, Escape pauses, and the pause menu includes Dev mode, Episode map and How to play.\n- Screenshots of the title, a room, a boss, the pause menu, the lobby and the About page look right after the layout fixes.\n\n**Not done, or only partly done against the TASK and plan**\n- **AI Hub online (shared-world netcode, session.js, the hub harness):** not built. The four hub-harness runs have not been attempted.\n- **Lightning Round:** not built.\n- **Art:** the sets are flat-coloured with neon accents. The outside dressing (bleachers, cranes, jumbotron) and the logo decal on the floor are not drawn. Enemy and boss art is simpler than the plan describes.\n- **Babble voices and music:** implemented, but I have not listened to them. The tunes are short loops.\n- **Recap, endings and Green Room:** functional but plain text and simple layouts. The Green Room paparazzi are basic.\n- **Attract mode:** ten reels with bots and cheats, but simpler captions and transitions than specified.\n- **Tests:** the suites cover core rules, input, contestant, weapons, economy, ratings, enemies, rooms, room sweep, bosses, playthrough, UI, dev, attract, touch, audio and proof. There are no net or hub suites. The browser checks are separate Python scripts, not part of the runner.\n- **Some plan items are not as described:** the keycap glyphs look dark in screenshots. I did not check the text sizing against a 1080p TV.\n- **Usage (API cost and tokens):** recorded as \"unknown\" in the exit interview and About screen.\n\n**Choices I made that you may want to change**\n- Engine patches were kept to three (P1, P3, P4); see `engine/PATCHES.md`. P2 (glyph default) was not needed because the game reads the engine's own `glyphs` setting.\n- Enemy and pickup randomness is seeded. Cosmetic randomness is left unseeded.\n- Feedback sections in the exit interview and About screen were written from my own session, so counts such as \"about 10 bugs found\" are approximate."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1033,"cache_read_input_tokens":566577,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1033},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eec69157-3f75-40b4-be93-e6ea9b3a321a","uuid":"4afb3ff5-1704-4442-8e7e-be4fb53de291","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:37:44.298Z","request_id":"req_011CghuACnDbCKkAuWWnCzUp"}
